WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.677 --> 00:00:05.017
Allah Uqba.

2
00:00:05.097 --> 00:00:07.837
Allah Uqba.

3
00:00:07.917 --> 00:00:10.737
Allah Uqba.

4
00:00:10.817 --> 00:00:11.817
Allah Uqba.

5
00:00:12.077 --> 00:00:13.977
Allah...

6
00:02:23.357 --> 00:02:27.217
I'm not interested in hearing
excuses about local conditions.

7
00:02:27.317 --> 00:02:29.637
No doubt they're local conditions.

8
00:02:29.897 --> 00:02:33.917
Here's a criminal whose exploits have
made him notorious throughout Europe.

9
00:02:33.997 --> 00:02:37.197
He escaped from France
with a fortune in jewels.

10
00:02:37.277 --> 00:02:41.277
And for two years, he's been living here
in Algiers, within a stone's throw of your

11
00:02:41.357 --> 00:02:43.057
headquarters. As you say, Commissioner.

12
00:02:43.137 --> 00:02:45.937
I'm here to settle this.
I want it done quickly.

13
00:02:46.017 --> 00:02:48.857
We've been trying to settle the
case of Pepe Lamoco for two years.

14
00:02:48.937 --> 00:02:51.857
In Paris, we handle more
difficult cases every day.

15
00:02:51.937 --> 00:02:54.277
Too bad you didn't arrest
him for escape from France.

16
00:02:54.357 --> 00:02:55.877
Nearly an oversight, no doubt.

17
00:02:55.957 --> 00:02:57.457
Do you deal in riddles here?

18
00:02:57.537 --> 00:02:59.097
Indeed we do.

19
00:02:59.177 --> 00:03:00.557
Oriental riddles.

20
00:03:00.677 --> 00:03:04.197
From my experience, there's no
problem in surrounding a given area.

21
00:03:04.277 --> 00:03:07.457
You close in and you make a
house-to-house investigation.

22
00:03:07.537 --> 00:03:10.117
The house to house investigation.

23
00:03:12.597 --> 00:03:14.357
You've just arrived from
the palace, Commissioner.

24
00:03:14.437 --> 00:03:15.797
You're not familiar with the Casbah.

25
00:03:15.877 --> 00:03:17.937
Casbah? What's that? Some kind of nut?

26
00:03:18.017 --> 00:03:19.697
A very hard nut to crack.

27
00:03:19.777 --> 00:03:21.957
You see, Pepe Lamoco lives in the Casbah.

28
00:03:22.037 --> 00:03:23.357
Why not go in? Take him out of it.

29
00:03:23.437 --> 00:03:25.057
You can't arrest a king in his own palace.

30
00:03:25.137 --> 00:03:26.917
Pepe's well guarded. Let me show you.

31
00:03:26.997 --> 00:03:28.437
Oh, it's fantastic.

32
00:03:28.517 --> 00:03:30.357
As a civilized man,
you don't like fantasy.

33
00:03:30.437 --> 00:03:32.517
As a police officer,
I don't believe in it.

34
00:03:32.597 --> 00:03:33.857
But here it is.

35
00:03:34.017 --> 00:03:36.537
The native porter known as the Casbah.

36
00:03:37.277 --> 00:03:39.257
You put it here, it's just
a few lines on the map.

37
00:03:39.337 --> 00:03:43.537
But the reality is something stranger
than anything you could have dreamed.

38
00:03:43.617 --> 00:03:46.297
It's only a step from the
modern city of the Caspar.

39
00:03:46.377 --> 00:03:49.257
But when you take that step,
you enter another world.

40
00:03:49.337 --> 00:03:52.317
A melting pot for all
the sins of the earth.

41
00:03:53.157 --> 00:03:56.757
Seen from a bird's eye view,
the Caspar is a great staircase.

42
00:03:56.937 --> 00:03:59.497
Each step is a terrace
rising from the sea.

43
00:03:59.737 --> 00:04:03.877
If you observe more closely, you'll see
that those terraces and courtyards and

44
00:04:03.957 --> 00:04:08.757
twisted streets are like a crawling
anthill, a jungle of houses,

45
00:04:08.837 --> 00:04:14.657
a labyrinth of narrow passages and winding
alleys, rotten with vermin and decay and

46
00:04:14.737 --> 00:04:16.277
the filth of centuries.

47
00:04:16.497 --> 00:04:20.077
No one knows what mysteries
are hidden behind those walls.

48
00:04:20.157 --> 00:04:24.897
No one knows what crimes and hopes
are buried in those secret courtyards.

49
00:04:25.077 --> 00:04:27.957
40,000 inhabitants
from all over the world.

50
00:04:28.157 --> 00:04:30.745
Some have been settled
here for generations.

51
00:04:31.177 --> 00:04:33.412
There are rebels in their white robes,

52
00:04:34.997 --> 00:04:37.657
gypsies with their
fortune-telling in their songs.

53
00:04:37.737 --> 00:04:42.517
There are many Czechos, there
are Slavs far from home, Maltese,

54
00:04:42.997 --> 00:04:45.297
Negroes from every corner of Africa,

55
00:04:45.577 --> 00:04:50.277
Sicilians and Spaniards, hot-blooded
and quick to hate, and women,

56
00:04:50.777 --> 00:04:55.917
women of every age and every shape,
women caught in the net of the Casbah.

57
00:04:56.077 --> 00:05:00.337
And everywhere there are terraces, all
connected together so that those who are

58
00:05:00.417 --> 00:05:03.757
accepted can move to
any part of the Casbah

59
00:05:04.777 --> 00:05:07.117
The terraces are the
domain of the native women.

60
00:05:07.197 --> 00:05:11.617
And it'd be death for a foreigner to go
there unless he were known and protected.

61
00:05:11.697 --> 00:05:15.077
The Casbah rises like
a fortress from the sea.

62
00:05:15.157 --> 00:05:17.797
Colorful, sordid, dangerous.

63
00:05:17.957 --> 00:05:20.617
There isn't just one Casbah.

64
00:05:20.697 --> 00:05:23.077
There are a hundred, a thousand.

65
00:05:23.237 --> 00:05:27.277
And in that labyrinth,
Pepe Lamoco is at home.

66
00:05:27.357 --> 00:05:29.777
And he's safe as long as he stays there.

67
00:05:29.857 --> 00:05:32.757
You mean to say that you
don't go into this quarter?

68
00:05:32.837 --> 00:05:34.697
It's easy to go in.

69
00:05:34.777 --> 00:05:37.657
Sometimes it's not so easy to come out.

70
00:05:37.737 --> 00:05:39.657
You cross the deadline.

71
00:05:39.737 --> 00:05:42.877
Suddenly, a bullet at your feet.

72
00:05:42.997 --> 00:05:45.957
It's just a friendly suggestion.

73
00:05:46.457 --> 00:05:49.117
Don't take the next step.

74
00:05:49.337 --> 00:05:52.457
From a roof up above, a voice speaks.

75
00:05:52.877 --> 00:05:54.277
Hello, Inspector.

76
00:05:54.357 --> 00:05:56.477
How did you know you were there?

77
00:05:56.557 --> 00:05:58.437
Don't ask us.

78
00:05:58.597 --> 00:06:00.997
Ask Inspector Slimane.

79
00:06:01.117 --> 00:06:03.857
The Casbah is his territory.

80
00:06:04.777 --> 00:06:06.157
He's a local concealed himself.

81
00:06:06.237 --> 00:06:07.757
Disguised, no doubt.

82
00:06:08.057 --> 00:06:09.497
You don't know Pepe.

83
00:06:09.577 --> 00:06:11.597
He'd laugh at the disguise.

84
00:06:11.737 --> 00:06:15.597
Why don't you find him? Oh,
but that is singularly easy.

85
00:06:15.677 --> 00:06:17.357
I see him every day.

86
00:06:17.437 --> 00:06:18.237
What?

87
00:06:18.317 --> 00:06:20.957
Our distinguished colleague is disturbed.

88
00:06:21.037 --> 00:06:25.077
The man is wanted in all the capitals
of Europe and you see him every day.

89
00:06:25.157 --> 00:06:28.157
Another example of what
you call local condition.

90
00:06:28.237 --> 00:06:30.717
Gross inefficiency.
No effort to make an arrest.

91
00:06:30.797 --> 00:06:34.477
To arrest him in the caspah,
distinguished colleague, would be simple.

92
00:06:34.557 --> 00:06:36.717
To get him out would be impossible.

93
00:06:36.797 --> 00:06:41.677
So you'd do nothing. I flatter myself
that I do a great deal in my humble way.

94
00:06:41.757 --> 00:06:44.177
I learn about Pepe. I know his habits.

95
00:06:44.257 --> 00:06:45.897
I study his weaknesses.

96
00:06:45.997 --> 00:06:49.757
When one can't use guns,
one must work with brains.

97
00:06:49.837 --> 00:06:51.337
I prefer guns.

98
00:06:51.417 --> 00:06:55.337
In your case, honored, sir,
such a preference is unavoidable.

99
00:06:55.417 --> 00:06:58.357
By his looks, I'd say he was
too lazy to make an arrest.

100
00:06:58.437 --> 00:06:59.897
I'm merely careful.

101
00:07:00.797 --> 00:07:02.557
that you're looking after your own skin.

102
00:07:02.637 --> 00:07:04.517
It's the only skin I have.

103
00:07:04.597 --> 00:07:06.737
So Pepe Lamoco wouldn't amuse me.

104
00:07:06.817 --> 00:07:08.277
We'll find out.

105
00:07:08.357 --> 00:07:11.237
I want 12 men tonight
inspected and ready for work.

106
00:07:11.317 --> 00:07:14.637
And you might prepare a
special cell for Pepe Lamoco.

107
00:07:14.717 --> 00:07:18.637
You and I have the same
feeling, Pepe, for beauty.

108
00:07:18.717 --> 00:07:22.257
This pearl belongs on a
very special kind of ear.

109
00:07:22.457 --> 00:07:27.077
Like a pink shell with a
little curl of gold hair.

110
00:07:27.157 --> 00:07:29.397
A special kind of gold.

111
00:07:36.777 --> 00:07:39.477
No, bells don't suit you at all, Carlos.

112
00:07:39.557 --> 00:07:42.437
You're not the type. He'd look
better with rings in his ears.

113
00:07:42.517 --> 00:07:45.497
Yes, and one in his nose.
He is definitely uncouth.

114
00:07:45.577 --> 00:07:47.397
You took the words out of my mouth.

115
00:07:47.477 --> 00:07:49.257
He's trying to cheat us, Pepe.

116
00:07:49.337 --> 00:07:51.677
All this talk is so he
can get a better price.

117
00:07:51.757 --> 00:07:53.657
So he can make fools of us.

118
00:07:54.257 --> 00:07:57.197
Yes, so easy to make a fool of me.

119
00:07:57.277 --> 00:07:59.042
Why don't you try it sometime?

120
00:07:59.357 --> 00:08:01.817
Grand-Père has dealt
with us for two years.

121
00:08:01.897 --> 00:08:03.777
We must have confidence in each other.

122
00:08:03.857 --> 00:08:05.217
That's the way to get along.

123
00:08:05.297 --> 00:08:09.826
That's the truth, Pepe. Well, why don't
we get our money and be done with it?

124
00:08:10.057 --> 00:08:12.057
He doesn't speak our language.

125
00:08:12.237 --> 00:08:15.317
Pretend he's not here. Yes, but I am here.

126
00:08:15.957 --> 00:08:17.717
He doesn't know he's not here.

127
00:08:17.797 --> 00:08:21.417
One more thing he doesn't know will
make it practically a perfect score.

128
00:08:21.497 --> 00:08:23.657
He was talking about beauty.

129
00:08:23.737 --> 00:08:28.217
The more he talks about beauty,
the less he talks about money.

130
00:08:28.477 --> 00:08:29.737
You're talking about how much.

131
00:08:29.817 --> 00:08:31.277
Oh, you make me sick.

132
00:08:31.357 --> 00:08:31.997
What?

133
00:08:32.077 --> 00:08:33.397
Say that again.

134
00:08:33.777 --> 00:08:35.577
You make me sick?

135
00:08:35.897 --> 00:08:37.777
Since you make him sick?

136
00:08:40.417 --> 00:08:41.417
Okay.

137
00:08:43.337 --> 00:08:45.297
Look, but don't touch.

138
00:08:45.377 --> 00:08:47.577
You know, this was once my trade.

139
00:08:47.657 --> 00:08:49.537
I began life in a jewelry store.

140
00:08:49.617 --> 00:08:51.697
And when you left, you
took the store with you?

141
00:08:51.777 --> 00:08:53.297
Yeah, it became a habit.

142
00:08:53.577 --> 00:08:55.717
You know, I dream about
settling down in Paris sometime.

143
00:08:55.797 --> 00:08:58.037
I'd make a collection of things like this.

144
00:08:58.117 --> 00:09:02.017
Not just for myself, for
people to see in glass cases.

145
00:09:02.297 --> 00:09:04.837
With you in a uniform
taking care of them, Gil.

146
00:09:04.917 --> 00:09:06.317
And you, Max.

147
00:09:06.897 --> 00:09:08.017
And me?

148
00:09:08.097 --> 00:09:09.517
You, Pierrot.

149
00:09:09.597 --> 00:09:11.737
Oh, you'd have a uniform like a general.

150
00:09:11.817 --> 00:09:13.717
And you'd be in charge of everything.

151
00:09:13.797 --> 00:09:15.277
What about me?

152
00:09:17.537 --> 00:09:19.017
What would he be?

153
00:09:19.657 --> 00:09:21.237
Stuffed in a glass case?

154
00:09:21.317 --> 00:09:22.277
What?

155
00:09:22.357 --> 00:09:28.437
Say that again! Stoked in a
glass case like an Egyptian mummy.

156
00:09:31.537 --> 00:09:33.077
Okay.

157
00:09:44.077 --> 00:09:45.397
Hey!

158
00:09:45.477 --> 00:09:46.397
Police!

159
00:09:46.477 --> 00:09:47.517
Police!

160
00:09:50.817 --> 00:09:51.877
Police!

161
00:09:51.957 --> 00:09:52.957
Police!

162
00:10:22.117 --> 00:10:24.377
You, where's Pepe Le Moncourt?

163
00:10:24.457 --> 00:10:26.577
Anna, my bank,

164
00:10:32.497 --> 00:10:33.597
or...

165
00:10:42.917 --> 00:10:43.997
Come here.

166
00:10:46.637 --> 00:10:48.777
Where's Pepe Le Moncourt? I don't know.

167
00:10:48.857 --> 00:10:50.877
By the sword of the great prophet,

168
00:10:51.937 --> 00:10:54.277
He hasn't let me look
on his face in two weeks.

169
00:10:54.357 --> 00:10:55.417
Let him go.

170
00:11:04.957 --> 00:11:05.777
Grandpere.

171
00:11:05.857 --> 00:11:08.057
Who's he? Receiver of stolen goods.

172
00:11:08.137 --> 00:11:09.277
You know where his place is?

173
00:11:09.357 --> 00:11:10.577
We know it.

174
00:11:32.737 --> 00:11:34.197
Pepe. No.

175
00:11:34.277 --> 00:11:35.277
It's me.

176
00:11:40.457 --> 00:11:42.297
What's the matter? The police.

177
00:11:42.377 --> 00:11:44.297
They're looking for Pepe. So soon?

178
00:11:44.377 --> 00:11:44.877
Soon?

179
00:11:44.937 --> 00:11:46.777
Were you expecting them? Always.

180
00:11:46.857 --> 00:11:48.257
But especially tonight.

181
00:11:48.337 --> 00:11:51.337
Pepe said they sent someone
all the way from Paris.

182
00:11:52.037 --> 00:11:54.297
Of course. Pepe knows everything.

183
00:11:54.377 --> 00:11:56.117
You're going to him?

184
00:11:56.197 --> 00:11:58.577
Tell him I've never seen so many of them.

185
00:11:58.657 --> 00:11:59.817
He'll laugh.

186
00:11:59.897 --> 00:12:01.717
That's what he expected. Look.

187
00:12:01.797 --> 00:12:02.797
Look at my neck.

188
00:12:02.877 --> 00:12:05.077
I thought they were going
to wring it like a chicken.

189
00:12:05.157 --> 00:12:07.157
But all the time I thought only of Pepe.

190
00:12:07.237 --> 00:12:08.797
But he killed me,
I thought, so long as Pepe.

191
00:12:08.877 --> 00:12:11.377
Why should you feel that way about Pepe?

192
00:12:12.337 --> 00:12:13.397
Don't you?

193
00:12:13.497 --> 00:12:14.497
I?

194
00:12:14.977 --> 00:12:17.377
Everyone knows how I feel about Pepe.

195
00:12:17.457 --> 00:12:20.817
Pepe doesn't like me.
He ignores me, humiliates me.

196
00:12:21.777 --> 00:12:24.097
Sometime he'll be sorry
he didn't notice me sooner.

197
00:12:24.177 --> 00:12:27.537
Oh, I'm very humble. I do my
best to serve him in my own way.

198
00:12:27.617 --> 00:12:28.957
That's nice of you, Regis.

199
00:12:29.037 --> 00:12:30.997
Well, that's how I am. Sensitive.

200
00:12:31.077 --> 00:12:32.497
But no one appreciates me.

201
00:12:32.577 --> 00:12:34.757
Promise me you'll tell him
that I came to warn him.

202
00:12:34.837 --> 00:12:37.157
I will. I don't want any favors.

203
00:12:37.237 --> 00:12:41.997
I only wanted to know that where
there's trouble, look for Regis.

204
00:13:00.917 --> 00:13:02.897
The third door on the left.

205
00:13:03.877 --> 00:13:05.937
Take three men and cover the roof.

206
00:13:09.297 --> 00:13:11.237
You men go around the back.

207
00:13:39.457 --> 00:13:42.157
I'm sorry.

208
00:14:26.497 --> 00:14:29.177
It's Isle, quick!

209
00:14:37.957 --> 00:14:39.377
The President?

210
00:14:39.457 --> 00:14:41.077
Police on the roof, Pepe.

211
00:14:41.157 --> 00:14:42.437
They're coming.

212
00:14:42.837 --> 00:14:44.077
They surrounded the house.

213
00:14:44.157 --> 00:14:45.451
They know you're here.

214
00:14:45.997 --> 00:14:47.317
That's funny.

215
00:14:47.657 --> 00:14:49.417
How did they know I was here?

216
00:14:49.497 --> 00:14:52.197
Oh, one can't meditate in peace anymore.

217
00:14:52.277 --> 00:14:54.337
Always rush and bustle.

218
00:14:54.417 --> 00:14:55.497
I'll take this one.

219
00:14:55.577 --> 00:14:56.757
I'd like it.

220
00:15:00.677 --> 00:15:02.337
You think that's a toy?

221
00:15:02.417 --> 00:15:04.652
When will you know it will be ordered?

222
00:15:07.877 --> 00:15:08.877
See?

223
00:15:09.297 --> 00:15:11.097
Don't take so many chances.

224
00:15:11.177 --> 00:15:12.237
That's foolish.

225
00:15:12.417 --> 00:15:16.535
I don't want a bullet to come between
us, the way that one almost hit.

226
00:15:34.197 --> 00:15:35.557
Break it down.

227
00:15:46.897 --> 00:15:49.857
Every few weeks I have to get new doors.

228
00:16:02.557 --> 00:16:04.897
Ines, did you tell anyone where I was?

229
00:16:04.977 --> 00:16:06.237
No one, Pepe.

230
00:16:06.317 --> 00:16:07.157
You're sure?

231
00:16:07.237 --> 00:16:08.197
Try to remember.

232
00:16:08.277 --> 00:16:09.857
Why don't you believe me, Pepe?

233
00:16:09.937 --> 00:16:11.737
All I want is to please you.

234
00:16:11.817 --> 00:16:13.677
I couldn't lie to you.

235
00:16:15.337 --> 00:16:16.457
Couldn't you?

236
00:16:16.677 --> 00:16:19.777
What about all that time you kept
telling me that you didn't like me?

237
00:16:19.857 --> 00:16:21.097
But this is serious.

238
00:16:21.177 --> 00:16:22.257
Ah, so?

239
00:16:22.337 --> 00:16:23.757
Love is not serious.

240
00:16:23.837 --> 00:16:25.977
Pepe, it's serious if
someone told the police.

241
00:16:26.057 --> 00:16:27.657
I didn't talk to anyone.

242
00:16:28.317 --> 00:16:29.417
Preaches came.

243
00:16:29.557 --> 00:16:30.577
Who came?

244
00:16:30.657 --> 00:16:31.657
Preaches.

245
00:16:32.017 --> 00:16:34.437
As soon as he told me, I'll enter you.

246
00:16:34.777 --> 00:16:36.197
What did he just tell you?

247
00:16:36.277 --> 00:16:39.257
About the police.
He wanted me to warn you.

248
00:16:39.337 --> 00:16:42.097
It was nice of him. That's what I thought.

249
00:16:43.057 --> 00:16:46.881
Is that all you thought? Was there
anything else for me to think?

250
00:16:47.897 --> 00:16:49.937
That's what I like about you.

251
00:16:50.037 --> 00:16:51.037
What?

252
00:16:52.597 --> 00:16:53.957
Never mind.

253
00:17:09.497 --> 00:17:10.917
This seems to be all.

254
00:17:10.997 --> 00:17:12.137
All for me.

255
00:17:12.217 --> 00:17:13.717
Search the place.

256
00:17:24.477 --> 00:17:26.117
Hold out your hand.

257
00:17:28.877 --> 00:17:30.697
Don't grab. It's unlucky.

258
00:17:30.777 --> 00:17:32.718
You want to give it to me, Beppe?

259
00:17:35.597 --> 00:17:38.457
No. It's for some fat old woman.

260
00:17:38.617 --> 00:17:40.057
Let me have it, Beppe.

261
00:17:40.137 --> 00:17:42.217
Sometime I'll get fat. Use it before that.

262
00:17:42.297 --> 00:17:42.997
No.

263
00:17:43.077 --> 00:17:44.697
I'll keep it for a charm.

264
00:17:44.777 --> 00:17:46.377
Then you must keep your fingers crossed.

265
00:17:46.457 --> 00:17:47.457
All right.

266
00:17:53.617 --> 00:17:54.617
So?

267
00:17:55.737 --> 00:17:59.397
This ring will mean that
I'm always yours, Pippi.

268
00:17:59.637 --> 00:18:01.417
Will my fingers cross?

269
00:18:05.077 --> 00:18:07.877
Those vantals are turning
my house upside down.

270
00:18:07.957 --> 00:18:10.251
They'll be in here next. Let's get out.

271
00:18:11.157 --> 00:18:14.863
Now, you stay here. When the
police come, you know what to say.

272
00:18:18.337 --> 00:18:20.217
No evidence? Nothing.

273
00:18:20.297 --> 00:18:23.017
Are you satisfied? I'm never satisfied.

274
00:18:24.637 --> 00:18:26.557
The rest of you follow me.

275
00:18:31.117 --> 00:18:32.477
There they go.

276
00:19:45.137 --> 00:19:46.617
This way, quick.

277
00:19:49.497 --> 00:19:50.617
Come in.

278
00:19:50.697 --> 00:19:52.117
Make yourself comfortable.

279
00:19:52.197 --> 00:19:53.577
What is this? What happened?

280
00:19:53.657 --> 00:19:54.817
Oh, it's nothing.

281
00:19:54.897 --> 00:19:56.457
You call this nothing?

282
00:19:56.537 --> 00:19:57.957
Oh, you know how the police are.

283
00:19:58.037 --> 00:19:59.777
They like to keep everything in an uproar.

284
00:19:59.857 --> 00:20:02.237
A very profound observation.

285
00:20:10.097 --> 00:20:13.097
The police have been trying
to catch him for two years.

286
00:20:13.177 --> 00:20:15.137
The police must be rather stupid.

287
00:20:15.217 --> 00:20:18.857
As one of them, I consider that
a triumph of understatement.

288
00:20:18.937 --> 00:20:21.617
You're one of them?
I have that doubtful honor.

289
00:20:21.697 --> 00:20:23.837
How does he do it? Good head.

290
00:20:23.917 --> 00:20:25.397
It's not his head that saves him.

291
00:20:25.477 --> 00:20:26.397
It's his heart.

292
00:20:26.477 --> 00:20:29.557
A man with such a good heart
could get around anyone.

293
00:20:29.637 --> 00:20:31.017
Sounds intriguing.

294
00:20:31.977 --> 00:20:33.797
That's a matter of taste.

295
00:20:37.357 --> 00:20:39.377
Oh, the inspector.

296
00:20:51.997 --> 00:20:53.457
Fix it up.

297
00:20:53.597 --> 00:20:56.177
Permit me to hope that
it's nothing serious.

298
00:20:56.257 --> 00:20:56.997
Thanks.

299
00:20:57.077 --> 00:20:58.477
A flea bite.

300
00:21:29.077 --> 00:21:31.517
Why aren't you chasing the fox?

301
00:21:31.597 --> 00:21:33.377
Oh, such a silly business.

302
00:21:33.457 --> 00:21:35.077
I prefer to use my brains.

303
00:21:35.157 --> 00:21:38.117
Well, your friends did a little
better than usual tonight.

304
00:21:38.197 --> 00:21:40.197
At least they found me.
That's pretty good for them.

305
00:21:40.277 --> 00:21:42.637
Shall we say a step
in the right direction?

306
00:21:42.717 --> 00:21:45.217
Excuse us, madame, if we talk shop.

307
00:21:45.357 --> 00:21:46.157
Cigarette?

308
00:21:46.237 --> 00:21:47.237
Please.

309
00:21:50.697 --> 00:21:51.697
Oh.

310
00:21:56.397 --> 00:21:57.837
Let me help you.

311
00:22:02.857 --> 00:22:05.957
So, they surrounded the house.

312
00:22:06.037 --> 00:22:07.057
Yes.

313
00:22:07.457 --> 00:22:09.937
They thought I was at Grand Pérez.

314
00:22:10.937 --> 00:22:12.157
Poor old man.

315
00:22:12.237 --> 00:22:15.817
He has no luck. They won't
even let him sleep in peace.

316
00:22:16.137 --> 00:22:18.157
Sometimes I feel sorry for them.

317
00:22:18.237 --> 00:22:20.337
They'll never get me by
this technique, you know.

318
00:22:20.417 --> 00:22:22.917
I've tried to point that out to them.

319
00:22:23.977 --> 00:22:27.257
For once we agree, the inspector and I.

320
00:22:27.337 --> 00:22:30.477
I am the one who will
get you, papé, in the end.

321
00:22:30.597 --> 00:22:32.717
I can hardly wait for the day.

322
00:22:32.797 --> 00:22:35.137
And not only you, but the others.

323
00:22:35.517 --> 00:22:38.277
Pierrot, Carlos, Grandpère, all of you.

324
00:22:38.357 --> 00:22:39.997
And then what will you do?

325
00:22:40.097 --> 00:22:41.697
Put us in the zoo?

326
00:22:41.777 --> 00:22:43.557
You flatter yourself.

327
00:22:43.937 --> 00:22:47.137
Oh, you mean, you won't show me in a cage?

328
00:22:47.217 --> 00:22:49.537
You're important now because you're free.

329
00:22:49.617 --> 00:22:53.077
Once you're behind bars,
people will forget all about you.

330
00:22:54.457 --> 00:22:56.757
He's funny, my friends, Slimane.

331
00:22:58.197 --> 00:23:00.457
But he has delusions of grandeur.

332
00:23:00.537 --> 00:23:01.977
He thinks he can arrest me.

333
00:23:02.057 --> 00:23:04.497
That's exactly what I'm gonna do, Pepe.

334
00:23:06.817 --> 00:23:09.517
Sure. Sure, sure, sure, sure.

335
00:23:10.497 --> 00:23:12.377
You make me laugh.

336
00:23:12.697 --> 00:23:14.177
You know what I like about you?

337
00:23:14.257 --> 00:23:16.877
No, but I'm humbly
waiting for you to tell me.

338
00:23:16.957 --> 00:23:21.037
Your face. It's a
perfect face for your job.

339
00:23:21.117 --> 00:23:24.457
To look that false is almost
the equivalent of being honest.

340
00:23:24.537 --> 00:23:27.297
I'm honored that my
appearance pleases you.

341
00:23:32.817 --> 00:23:34.317
You excuse me.

342
00:23:34.397 --> 00:23:36.177
I'm afraid I have to go.

343
00:23:36.857 --> 00:23:37.917
Business.

344
00:23:43.057 --> 00:23:44.617
Good luck, Pepe.

345
00:23:49.857 --> 00:23:51.377
It's a shame, isn't it?

346
00:23:51.457 --> 00:23:52.117
What?

347
00:23:52.197 --> 00:23:55.457
A waste of talent,
an unusual intelligence.

348
00:23:55.537 --> 00:23:57.817
One hates to see him buried so easily.

349
00:23:58.097 --> 00:24:00.397
Therein? It's the same thing.

350
00:24:00.597 --> 00:24:02.677
What makes you so sure?

351
00:24:02.877 --> 00:24:06.917
I've marked the date of his
arrest on the wall of my room.

352
00:24:07.017 --> 00:24:08.177
High.

353
00:24:08.277 --> 00:24:12.177
Where it reads black in
the rays of the setting sun.

354
00:24:13.097 --> 00:24:14.597
Shall we go?

355
00:24:20.617 --> 00:24:25.957
And although we narrowly missed capturing
Pepe Lemoco, he was evidently wounded

356
00:24:26.037 --> 00:24:27.077
while escaping.

357
00:24:27.157 --> 00:24:30.197
In fact, his injuries may prove fatal.

358
00:24:30.437 --> 00:24:34.797
In the event of his death,
I shall inform you without delay.

359
00:24:34.877 --> 00:24:37.017
Why don't you just declare
him dead and be done with it?

360
00:24:37.097 --> 00:24:42.037
You may rest assured that I have the
situation well in hand and will take whatever

361
00:24:42.117 --> 00:24:43.937
steps I deem advisable.

362
00:24:44.017 --> 00:24:45.997
Wire that to Paris immediately.

363
00:24:52.417 --> 00:24:55.377
What does he mean by saying he
has the situation well in hand?

364
00:24:55.457 --> 00:24:59.217
He means he's going to sit here and write
letters to Paris while he waits for Pepe

365
00:24:59.297 --> 00:25:02.917
to die of old age. That's better than
going into the Caspar looking for him.

366
00:25:02.997 --> 00:25:05.977
At least our friend from Paris has
learned something about the Caspar.

367
00:25:06.057 --> 00:25:08.817
We've all learned that there's
only one way to arrest Pepe.

368
00:25:08.897 --> 00:25:10.877
Oh, that's very intelligent of you.

369
00:25:10.957 --> 00:25:13.077
As you know, my intelligence
is at your service.

370
00:25:13.157 --> 00:25:14.877
Well, so far it's hardly been enough.

371
00:25:14.957 --> 00:25:17.797
Ah, but it's not enough. But wait,
suppose Pepe comes out of the caspar,

372
00:25:17.877 --> 00:25:20.277
then it follows his arrest
as a matter of child's play.

373
00:25:20.357 --> 00:25:22.557
Shall we send him an engraved invitation?

374
00:25:22.637 --> 00:25:23.377
Huh?

375
00:25:23.457 --> 00:25:24.457
Oh.

376
00:25:25.037 --> 00:25:26.877
Pepe's too clever to fall into a trap.

377
00:25:26.957 --> 00:25:29.337
But some of his friends are not so clever.

378
00:25:29.417 --> 00:25:33.357
Get to the point. Now, suppose
Piero comes down into the town.

379
00:25:33.437 --> 00:25:36.937
Pepe will be worried by his absence and
he'll come down into the town to find him.

380
00:25:37.017 --> 00:25:38.557
You overlook just one little point.

381
00:25:38.637 --> 00:25:40.217
How do you get Piero to come down?

382
00:25:40.297 --> 00:25:41.957
Ah, that's my plan.

383
00:25:42.037 --> 00:25:43.897
A magnificent plan.

384
00:25:44.217 --> 00:25:46.217
I have here a letter.

385
00:25:46.297 --> 00:25:47.897
I got it from Piero.

386
00:25:47.977 --> 00:25:49.377
But he doesn't know that.

387
00:25:49.457 --> 00:25:50.657
The letter's from his mother.

388
00:25:50.737 --> 00:25:52.777
A letter of exquisite tenderness.

389
00:25:52.857 --> 00:25:54.157
From France.

390
00:25:54.937 --> 00:25:56.257
Can't see much value in that.

391
00:25:56.337 --> 00:25:58.197
He's a bad boy, but a good son.

392
00:25:58.277 --> 00:26:01.177
So it isn't the good son that
we'll lock up, but the bad boy.

393
00:26:01.257 --> 00:26:04.957
Then we keep the arrest a secret, and Papi
will come down out of the Casbah to look

394
00:26:05.037 --> 00:26:05.897
for Piero.

395
00:26:05.977 --> 00:26:06.977
Ah.

396
00:26:07.817 --> 00:26:08.917
We agreed?

397
00:26:10.157 --> 00:26:11.157
Agreed.

398
00:26:13.497 --> 00:26:17.417
And as to the price, you know
the reward's being posted.

399
00:26:17.497 --> 00:26:21.297
Oh, but a little bonus besides
in view of the circumstances.

400
00:26:21.817 --> 00:26:22.837
Agreed.

401
00:26:23.737 --> 00:26:27.657
How do we know we can trust you not
to make a better bargain with Pepe?

402
00:26:27.737 --> 00:26:30.817
I'm an informer, not a hypocrite.

403
00:26:32.357 --> 00:26:33.777
What are you laughing at?

404
00:26:33.857 --> 00:26:37.577
It amuses me to see you sell
your friends at bargain prices.

405
00:26:37.657 --> 00:26:40.097
You have a flair for business, Regis.

406
00:26:42.277 --> 00:26:44.097
He says that because he's jealous.

407
00:26:44.177 --> 00:26:45.537
It doesn't upset me.

408
00:26:45.777 --> 00:26:47.557
I ignore him.

409
00:27:01.537 --> 00:27:03.457
Oh, oh, oh.

410
00:27:08.477 --> 00:27:10.897
Double him, girl. He'll never make it.

411
00:27:14.017 --> 00:27:15.377
Good morning, Tanya.

412
00:27:15.457 --> 00:27:17.957
Good morning, Inspector.
And how is Carlos?

413
00:27:18.037 --> 00:27:22.597
Oh, what's he been? Don't tell me a
charming husband has been beating you again.

414
00:27:22.677 --> 00:27:24.337
You know how it is with a man.

415
00:27:24.417 --> 00:27:26.077
Well, I can't say I do.

416
00:27:26.157 --> 00:27:28.197
They seem to take to it naturally.

417
00:27:33.277 --> 00:27:34.537
Good morning, Freddy.

418
00:27:34.617 --> 00:27:36.157
Good morning, Pepe.

419
00:27:36.297 --> 00:27:37.917
Good morning, Pepe.

420
00:27:38.257 --> 00:27:39.277
Hello.

421
00:27:41.097 --> 00:27:42.377
Good morning.

422
00:27:42.577 --> 00:27:44.037
Better watch out, Pepe.

423
00:27:44.117 --> 00:27:45.617
Women will be the death of you.

424
00:27:45.697 --> 00:27:46.797
It's a happy day.

425
00:27:46.877 --> 00:27:48.277
Just warning you.

426
00:27:48.357 --> 00:27:50.317
Don't worry, I'll keep my head.

427
00:27:51.577 --> 00:27:53.517
I may need it one of these days.

428
00:27:53.597 --> 00:27:54.517
No doubt.

429
00:27:54.597 --> 00:27:56.717
Coming my way? With pleasure.

430
00:28:02.357 --> 00:28:03.837
Good morning, Pepe.

431
00:28:03.917 --> 00:28:04.917
Good morning.

432
00:28:05.977 --> 00:28:07.717
Good morning, Pepe.

433
00:28:07.797 --> 00:28:09.217
Good morning.

434
00:28:09.877 --> 00:28:12.017
Did you get home safely last night?

435
00:28:12.097 --> 00:28:13.277
Why not?

436
00:28:15.817 --> 00:28:17.317
Nothing unpleasant?

437
00:28:17.477 --> 00:28:20.257
Yes, we had one rather
unpleasant experience.

438
00:28:20.337 --> 00:28:20.837
Yeah?

439
00:28:20.917 --> 00:28:21.877
With you.

440
00:28:21.957 --> 00:28:24.897
She didn't think so.
What makes you so sure?

441
00:28:24.977 --> 00:28:27.877
Well, you know, women,
they talk about nothing.

442
00:28:27.957 --> 00:28:29.257
I hardly listen.

443
00:28:29.477 --> 00:28:32.217
Was there anything special about her?

444
00:28:32.297 --> 00:28:33.357
Yes.

445
00:28:33.457 --> 00:28:34.357
Pearls.

446
00:28:34.437 --> 00:28:36.337
The color I like.

447
00:28:36.817 --> 00:28:38.577
Handcuffs I can appreciate.

448
00:28:38.657 --> 00:28:40.217
Platinum and diamonds.

449
00:28:40.337 --> 00:28:43.057
And she didn't buy
that perfume in Algiers.

450
00:28:43.137 --> 00:28:46.217
So all you noticed were
the jewels and perfume.

451
00:28:46.297 --> 00:28:47.577
Was there anything else?

452
00:28:47.657 --> 00:28:49.197
What about the eyes?

453
00:28:49.277 --> 00:28:51.157
Well, they all have eyes.

454
00:28:51.237 --> 00:28:54.677
But all that tishy and jingle, you
don't see much of that in the Casbah.

455
00:28:54.757 --> 00:28:56.797
But you do where she comes from.

456
00:29:02.797 --> 00:29:05.577
She asked quite a few questions about you.

457
00:29:05.657 --> 00:29:06.597
Yeah?

458
00:29:06.677 --> 00:29:08.037
What did you tell her?

459
00:29:08.117 --> 00:29:09.517
What could I tell her?

460
00:29:09.597 --> 00:29:10.557
Why?

461
00:29:10.637 --> 00:29:12.757
You think she might be afraid of my past?

462
00:29:12.837 --> 00:29:16.077
No, but she might be a little
appalled at your future.

463
00:29:16.157 --> 00:29:19.097
I told her you might get off
for 20 years with a good lawyer.

464
00:29:19.177 --> 00:29:21.357
Oh, you wouldn't want me to get 20 years.

465
00:29:21.437 --> 00:29:22.937
You're too far to be.

466
00:29:23.137 --> 00:29:24.237
What's her name?

467
00:29:24.317 --> 00:29:26.897
So, you're thinking about her.

468
00:29:27.957 --> 00:29:30.377
About her when I don't know her name.

469
00:29:35.217 --> 00:29:37.377
Good morning, Pessie. Hello, Aisha.

470
00:29:37.457 --> 00:29:39.597
You go at home? No, is it Chinese?

471
00:29:39.797 --> 00:29:41.177
Let's go to Chinese.

472
00:29:44.417 --> 00:29:45.877
What do you want?

473
00:29:46.717 --> 00:29:48.917
Oh, I have a letter from Pierrot.

474
00:29:48.997 --> 00:29:51.137
Give it to me. Oh, no, no, no.

475
00:29:51.217 --> 00:29:55.797
I can't. I swore by the bones of my
ancestors to give it only to Pierrot.

476
00:29:55.877 --> 00:29:57.357
Who's the letter from?

477
00:29:58.717 --> 00:30:00.237
What kind of a woman?

478
00:30:00.317 --> 00:30:04.082
I didn't look. Well, you tell
the woman I took it away from you.

479
00:30:15.617 --> 00:30:20.337
This vulgar game is hardly worth the
compromise to one's dignity involved in playing

480
00:30:20.417 --> 00:30:21.037
it.

481
00:30:21.117 --> 00:30:22.537
It's vulgar, but it's fast.

482
00:30:22.617 --> 00:30:27.837
I don't know why I waste my time in
such common pursuits with such mediocre

483
00:30:27.917 --> 00:30:29.277
companions.

484
00:30:30.897 --> 00:30:37.097
By youth, I intended to become
a statesman or a philosopher.

485
00:30:37.657 --> 00:30:41.017
But a man's destiny is
written in the stars.

486
00:30:53.757 --> 00:30:58.717
We play the game, but
fate controls the cards.

487
00:30:58.797 --> 00:30:59.937
Who?

488
00:31:00.057 --> 00:31:01.277
Fate.

489
00:31:02.117 --> 00:31:07.617
If fate goes on controlling the cards,
he might find a knife between his ribs.

490
00:31:16.037 --> 00:31:18.617
The moving finger writes,

491
00:31:20.137 --> 00:31:23.297
And having writ moves on.

492
00:31:23.377 --> 00:31:24.997
Stop that nonsense.

493
00:31:25.617 --> 00:31:28.877
He has an ear, but not for poetry.

494
00:31:28.957 --> 00:31:30.457
I'm trying to think.

495
00:31:38.157 --> 00:31:40.237
I would have played the ace.

496
00:31:41.977 --> 00:31:43.497
You smell something?

497
00:31:43.577 --> 00:31:44.977
I've been wondering.

498
00:31:45.197 --> 00:31:46.657
Onions. Cheese.

499
00:31:48.117 --> 00:31:52.437
I don't like it. Would it be too much to
ask you to take your nose out of my hand?

500
00:31:52.517 --> 00:31:54.117
But you haven't got a hand.

501
00:31:54.197 --> 00:31:55.857
And don't blow down my back.

502
00:31:55.937 --> 00:31:57.297
You seem nervous.

503
00:31:57.477 --> 00:32:02.097
My dear fellow, consider
yourself blackballed by this club.

504
00:32:02.177 --> 00:32:04.077
Huh? He means get out.

505
00:32:05.237 --> 00:32:06.237
Oh.

506
00:32:09.497 --> 00:32:10.837
What are you hanging around for?

507
00:32:10.917 --> 00:32:11.977
This is business.

508
00:32:15.217 --> 00:32:17.537
Read this. Bad news?

509
00:32:19.497 --> 00:32:20.497
Pierrot.

510
00:32:21.097 --> 00:32:22.317
Wait for me.

511
00:32:27.477 --> 00:32:31.577
I would like it better if you didn't
hang around so much with Regis.

512
00:32:31.657 --> 00:32:32.657
Why?

513
00:32:33.857 --> 00:32:37.717
Did you ever see a clock that
pointed to two and struck four?

514
00:32:37.797 --> 00:32:39.997
Well, it is really a quarter past twelve.

515
00:32:40.077 --> 00:32:42.777
Well, your friend Regis is like that.

516
00:32:43.037 --> 00:32:44.717
He doesn't ring two.

517
00:32:44.897 --> 00:32:47.485
That's what you say,
but you can't prove it.

518
00:32:48.117 --> 00:32:50.957
I say so, that's enough. Well,
he just gets along all right with me.

519
00:32:51.037 --> 00:32:52.757
Well, that's why I'm
telling you, I don't like it.

520
00:32:52.837 --> 00:32:55.177
Well, I do. In business,
I'll do anything you say, Pepe.

521
00:32:55.257 --> 00:32:57.728
But outside business, I'll do as I please.

522
00:32:58.257 --> 00:32:59.477
Oh, so.

523
00:33:01.377 --> 00:33:03.057
You'll do as you please.

524
00:33:07.997 --> 00:33:09.797
It's a good thing I like you.

525
00:33:10.277 --> 00:33:11.397
Now get out.

526
00:33:17.097 --> 00:33:18.197
Nice gift.

527
00:33:20.477 --> 00:33:22.217
What did she write you in her last letter?

528
00:33:22.297 --> 00:33:25.037
She had a cold. She said she'd
start as soon as she felt better.

529
00:33:25.117 --> 00:33:26.497
Ah, then you knew she was coming.

530
00:33:26.577 --> 00:33:29.417
I sent her a money order. Well,
in that case, it isn't so strange.

531
00:33:29.497 --> 00:33:31.997
And yet it's odd that she should
arrive in Algiers like that,

532
00:33:32.077 --> 00:33:34.057
without letting you know.
That's what I thought.

533
00:33:34.137 --> 00:33:35.077
Ah!

534
00:33:35.157 --> 00:33:36.517
Is this her handwriting?

535
00:33:36.597 --> 00:33:38.077
Have you another letter on it?

536
00:33:38.157 --> 00:33:40.057
Yes, I think so. Good.

537
00:33:41.017 --> 00:33:42.897
like a pair of Siamese twins.

538
00:33:42.977 --> 00:33:45.918
Then we'll see if they're
both from the same mama.

539
00:33:49.657 --> 00:33:50.537
Hmm?

540
00:33:50.617 --> 00:33:53.757
Well, what do you think?
Same mistakes in spelling.

541
00:33:54.177 --> 00:33:56.517
Our poor dear mamas can never spell.

542
00:33:56.597 --> 00:33:58.177
Same M. Same what?

543
00:33:58.257 --> 00:33:59.077
Same M.

544
00:33:59.157 --> 00:34:00.597
And the crossing of the T.

545
00:34:00.677 --> 00:34:03.597
Well, that's settled. You
can always tell by the T.

546
00:34:03.677 --> 00:34:04.777
And you think it's all right?

547
00:34:04.857 --> 00:34:06.817
Well, you can see with your own eyes.

548
00:34:06.897 --> 00:34:08.517
Then I don't want her
to be there worrying.

549
00:34:08.597 --> 00:34:10.097
After all, she's 62.

550
00:34:11.217 --> 00:34:13.805
She never felt better
than the day she died.

551
00:34:14.397 --> 00:34:15.857
Rue de la Beauvoir.

552
00:34:16.097 --> 00:34:18.937
Where's that? Oh, I know
it well half-hour's walk.

553
00:34:19.017 --> 00:34:21.311
I can take you there if you wish to go.

554
00:34:22.197 --> 00:34:23.917
I've got to go. I've got to see you.

555
00:34:23.997 --> 00:34:25.737
Fortunately, you can rely on me.

556
00:34:25.817 --> 00:34:27.317
It's good of you to help me, Regis.

557
00:34:27.397 --> 00:34:29.177
You're a real friend.
Well, that's how I am.

558
00:34:29.257 --> 00:34:30.257
Saint-sident.

559
00:34:46.257 --> 00:34:47.777
You ready, Gabby?

560
00:34:47.857 --> 00:34:50.777
Andre just phoned. They're
waiting on the terrace.

561
00:34:50.857 --> 00:34:52.997
About five minutes, Andre phoned.

562
00:34:53.077 --> 00:34:55.724
Well, don't you like
having him so attentive?

563
00:34:56.197 --> 00:34:57.397
Love it.

564
00:34:58.117 --> 00:35:02.437
I've just been sitting here thinking
that I'm the happiest girl in the world.

565
00:35:02.517 --> 00:35:03.937
Well, you ought to be.

566
00:35:04.017 --> 00:35:07.377
Marrying a man who adores you and can
give you everything in the world you ever

567
00:35:07.457 --> 00:35:08.597
dreamed about.

568
00:35:08.977 --> 00:35:10.537
That's my trouble.

569
00:35:10.897 --> 00:35:12.317
I'm such a fool.

570
00:35:12.617 --> 00:35:15.017
I go dreaming about the wrong things.

571
00:35:15.097 --> 00:35:17.137
Well, that's a terrible mistake.

572
00:35:17.297 --> 00:35:18.417
Marie,

573
00:35:18.777 --> 00:35:22.197
remember the time in the
Banton bargain basement?

574
00:35:22.277 --> 00:35:26.457
The two of us behind the counter,
handkerchief, gloves, hose wheel?

575
00:35:26.677 --> 00:35:28.797
And don't you forget it.

576
00:35:31.667 --> 00:35:32.897
I won't.

577
00:35:37.237 --> 00:35:39.957
After all, you don't marry for fun.

578
00:35:42.957 --> 00:35:44.597
Hello, Inspector.

579
00:35:44.857 --> 00:35:46.237
Oh, you have already met.

580
00:35:46.317 --> 00:35:48.677
I took the liberty of presenting myself.

581
00:35:48.797 --> 00:35:52.937
As you see, I couldn't wait to take
advantage of your invitation last night.

582
00:35:53.017 --> 00:35:53.997
I'm glad.

583
00:35:54.077 --> 00:35:55.717
Yes, we're all glad.

584
00:35:56.357 --> 00:36:00.857
Inspector, will you tell my fiancé where
I was last night during the shooting?

585
00:36:00.937 --> 00:36:02.157
But with me.

586
00:36:02.237 --> 00:36:03.177
There you see.

587
00:36:03.257 --> 00:36:04.737
And who did we meet?

588
00:36:04.817 --> 00:36:07.217
Pepe Lamoco. Nice friends you have.

589
00:36:07.297 --> 00:36:09.717
In business one can't choose.

590
00:36:09.897 --> 00:36:10.817
You don't need Pepe Lamoco.

591
00:36:10.897 --> 00:36:13.237
Pepe Lamoco, the famous criminal?

592
00:36:13.737 --> 00:36:15.377
The one they're all talking about?

593
00:36:15.457 --> 00:36:16.957
He'd like to hear you say that.

594
00:36:17.037 --> 00:36:18.717
Just a common law-breaker.

595
00:36:20.137 --> 00:36:21.697
Have you seen him sing?

596
00:36:21.777 --> 00:36:22.777
Uh-huh.

597
00:36:23.077 --> 00:36:24.197
This morning.

598
00:36:24.277 --> 00:36:26.137
Did he say anything about me?

599
00:36:26.217 --> 00:36:28.097
Well, in a way.

600
00:36:28.217 --> 00:36:29.597
Oh, I know.

601
00:36:29.677 --> 00:36:30.917
My pearls.

602
00:36:30.997 --> 00:36:34.577
The connoisseur can admire pearls
without neglecting the wearer.

603
00:36:34.657 --> 00:36:38.363
Oh, he means if he stole your
pearls, he'd steal you with them.

604
00:36:38.457 --> 00:36:40.398
Doesn't that frighten you, Gabby?

605
00:36:40.897 --> 00:36:42.797
He's marvelous to me.
I'd like to meet him.

606
00:36:42.877 --> 00:36:44.857
It can easily be arranged.

607
00:36:45.417 --> 00:36:49.337
If you wish to visit the Casper
again with a suitable guide.

608
00:36:49.417 --> 00:36:51.337
How's that Andre? An adventure?

609
00:36:51.417 --> 00:36:53.137
Well, that's what we're here for.

610
00:36:53.217 --> 00:36:55.917
Once is enough for me.
I don't like natives.

611
00:36:56.057 --> 00:36:57.517
And we'll go with Maxime.

612
00:36:57.597 --> 00:36:59.337
You'll protect us, won't you Maxime?

613
00:36:59.417 --> 00:37:02.297
Oh, I'm at my best among natives.

614
00:37:03.917 --> 00:37:06.357
Tonight, Inspector, if it's convenient?

615
00:37:06.437 --> 00:37:07.437
Mm-hmm.

616
00:37:08.257 --> 00:37:09.257
Pepe!

617
00:37:10.897 --> 00:37:12.057
What are you doing?

618
00:37:12.257 --> 00:37:13.317
Nothing.

619
00:37:23.577 --> 00:37:25.917
What are you looking at like that?

620
00:37:25.997 --> 00:37:26.937
France.

621
00:37:27.017 --> 00:37:28.997
You can't see France.

622
00:37:29.677 --> 00:37:31.817
Well, there is no harm in trying.

623
00:37:32.337 --> 00:37:34.697
Pepe, what are you looking at like that?

624
00:37:34.777 --> 00:37:35.957
A ship.

625
00:37:36.777 --> 00:37:39.457
Doesn't it make it easy to look at boats?

626
00:37:40.897 --> 00:37:42.257
Do you like to ask so many questions?

627
00:37:42.337 --> 00:37:43.337
No.

628
00:37:43.617 --> 00:37:45.077
Why, have you got a headache?

629
00:37:45.157 --> 00:37:47.497
Oh, no, I'm thinking.

630
00:37:48.697 --> 00:37:51.109
Well, that's sure to give you a headache?

631
00:37:51.557 --> 00:37:54.317
I don't think with my
head, but with my heart.

632
00:37:54.397 --> 00:37:55.737
Then you'd better tell me.

633
00:37:55.817 --> 00:37:56.717
It's nothing.

634
00:37:56.797 --> 00:37:58.377
If it's nothing, you'd better tell me.

635
00:37:58.457 --> 00:38:00.677
Oh, I'll get mad if you go on like this.

636
00:38:00.757 --> 00:38:05.639
I want you to get mad. Shout at me, hurt
me, but don't treat me as if I'm not here.

637
00:38:06.377 --> 00:38:07.757
Oh, I know you're here.

638
00:38:07.837 --> 00:38:09.177
No, you don't.

639
00:38:16.477 --> 00:38:20.977
You are dreaming about something
with your eyes wide open.

640
00:38:23.737 --> 00:38:26.617
I wish you'd dream about me.

641
00:38:27.177 --> 00:38:30.217
Look, you've always lived in the Casbah.

642
00:38:30.297 --> 00:38:32.517
For you there is nothing outside.

643
00:38:32.837 --> 00:38:34.717
The Casbah's big enough.

644
00:38:34.797 --> 00:38:36.037
Not for me.

645
00:38:36.197 --> 00:38:37.877
It's like being in a grave.

646
00:38:37.957 --> 00:38:38.757
Pepe.

647
00:38:38.837 --> 00:38:40.877
I understand much more of it.

648
00:38:40.957 --> 00:38:43.657
If you want to go away, I'll go with you.

649
00:38:45.617 --> 00:38:46.617
Thanks.

650
00:38:48.117 --> 00:38:49.637
Won't you take me?

651
00:38:49.737 --> 00:38:51.297
I wish I could.

652
00:38:54.217 --> 00:38:55.857
Paris is a long way off.

653
00:38:55.937 --> 00:38:57.157
I don't care.

654
00:38:57.637 --> 00:38:59.217
It's different there.

655
00:39:01.437 --> 00:39:04.317
Couldn't you be happy with me in Paris?

656
00:39:08.797 --> 00:39:11.537
You think I look funny in Paris.

657
00:39:12.537 --> 00:39:15.277
Answer me! But it isn't you, Ines.

658
00:39:15.357 --> 00:39:16.437
It's the Casper.

659
00:39:16.517 --> 00:39:18.077
You belong here.

660
00:39:18.317 --> 00:39:20.199
You don't understand who I feel.

661
00:39:21.717 --> 00:39:23.937
I've studied for two years.

662
00:39:24.137 --> 00:39:26.897
The time comes when
you can't stand anymore.

663
00:39:27.437 --> 00:39:29.657
Morning, noon, and night.

664
00:39:29.817 --> 00:39:31.877
The same things, the same people.

665
00:39:31.957 --> 00:39:33.777
I'm fed up. I've had enough.

666
00:39:33.857 --> 00:39:35.217
You're tired of me.

667
00:39:35.297 --> 00:39:37.121
There's nothing to do with you.

668
00:39:39.197 --> 00:39:41.417
That has nothing to do with me.

669
00:39:42.657 --> 00:39:44.737
Do you know when you're going away?

670
00:39:44.817 --> 00:39:46.137
Never. You'll see.

671
00:39:46.217 --> 00:39:47.717
You can't do it.

672
00:39:47.797 --> 00:39:48.797
Never.

673
00:39:49.537 --> 00:39:51.517
I am the casbah. I'll keep you.

674
00:39:51.597 --> 00:39:54.009
Just try to get away and you'll find out.

675
00:39:54.517 --> 00:39:57.377
It's funny what the police have
come in and tried to arrest you.

676
00:39:57.457 --> 00:39:58.817
You're in prison already.

677
00:39:58.897 --> 00:40:01.097
You're in the casbah
with the wall around you.

678
00:40:01.177 --> 00:40:03.217
There's nothing else.
You'll never have anything else.

679
00:40:03.297 --> 00:40:05.257
I'll tell you. I am glad.

680
00:40:05.337 --> 00:40:07.117
There is no France for you.

681
00:40:08.337 --> 00:40:09.777
Are you full? No!

682
00:40:44.757 --> 00:40:46.377
Who is it?

683
00:40:46.517 --> 00:40:47.497
You?

684
00:40:47.577 --> 00:40:49.317
It's me, Archer.

685
00:41:08.657 --> 00:41:11.737
Oh, Pepe, I don't know what to do.

686
00:41:11.817 --> 00:41:14.437
Piero, I can't find him.

687
00:41:14.557 --> 00:41:19.657
Did you go to Chenise? Yes, and I went
to Mother Teches and the Alibaba and the

688
00:41:19.737 --> 00:41:20.977
Algerians.

689
00:41:21.077 --> 00:41:22.137
Everywhere.

690
00:41:22.237 --> 00:41:23.977
He ought to be back by now.

691
00:41:24.057 --> 00:41:24.597
Back?

692
00:41:24.677 --> 00:41:26.497
From the Rue du L'Aubrivoir.

693
00:41:26.777 --> 00:41:27.557
Good.

694
00:41:27.637 --> 00:41:29.317
Why did he go into town?

695
00:41:29.397 --> 00:41:30.917
To see his mother.

696
00:41:33.517 --> 00:41:35.477
What do you mean, to see his mother?

697
00:41:35.557 --> 00:41:37.277
He got a letter from her.

698
00:41:38.337 --> 00:41:39.617
And then he went down with Regis.

699
00:41:39.697 --> 00:41:42.577
And then Regis came back, but Pio...

700
00:41:42.657 --> 00:41:45.137
I'm still waiting for him, that's all.

701
00:41:46.677 --> 00:41:49.097
Where's Regis? At the Algerians.

702
00:41:49.197 --> 00:41:50.777
No need to go down.

703
00:41:51.397 --> 00:41:52.717
Here, thanks.

704
00:42:03.477 --> 00:42:04.717
See you later.

705
00:42:09.157 --> 00:42:10.897
Hello, Edges. What's your hurry?

706
00:42:10.977 --> 00:42:12.497
Oh, I'm in no hurry. Good.

707
00:42:12.577 --> 00:42:14.877
Then come along with me.
I'm waiting for Pio.

708
00:42:14.957 --> 00:42:16.137
We can wait for him together.

709
00:42:16.217 --> 00:42:18.037
But listen, Pepe, I've got to go down.

710
00:42:18.117 --> 00:42:18.857
What's the matter?

711
00:42:18.937 --> 00:42:20.217
What makes you so nervous?

712
00:42:20.297 --> 00:42:22.337
Me? Nervous? Why should I be nervous?

713
00:42:22.417 --> 00:42:23.597
Adjust it. Why?

714
00:42:23.677 --> 00:42:26.897
Well, it's only that usually you
hardly say hello to me when you do,

715
00:42:26.977 --> 00:42:28.757
so I don't expect it when you don't.

716
00:42:28.837 --> 00:42:31.197
I'm a little surprised when you
do because you don't usually...

717
00:42:31.277 --> 00:42:34.557
Well, you see, I haven't
appreciated you at your real value.

718
00:42:34.637 --> 00:42:37.117
That's the trouble. So I made a mistake.

719
00:42:37.197 --> 00:42:38.197
Shall we go?

720
00:42:38.337 --> 00:42:41.057
Where? Oh, in a quiet
corner where we can talk.

721
00:42:41.137 --> 00:42:43.957
I've been hearing great
stories about your courage.

722
00:42:44.037 --> 00:42:45.177
My courage?

723
00:42:45.257 --> 00:42:46.637
You're surprised?

724
00:42:46.717 --> 00:42:47.577
No.

725
00:42:47.657 --> 00:42:49.277
I even hear you've proved it.

726
00:42:49.357 --> 00:42:52.837
Me? Yes, you. Well, it's possible.

727
00:42:52.917 --> 00:42:54.897
One can be brave without knowing it.

728
00:42:54.977 --> 00:42:56.177
Of course.

729
00:42:57.497 --> 00:42:59.637
How did I prove it?

730
00:42:59.717 --> 00:43:02.337
Why, by going down into town with Pio.

731
00:43:02.417 --> 00:43:05.177
Ah, not everybody would have done that.

732
00:43:05.397 --> 00:43:06.897
Oh, yes.

733
00:43:08.937 --> 00:43:10.897
That was a brave thing to do.

734
00:43:10.977 --> 00:43:13.137
Yes, of course wasn't it.

735
00:43:16.037 --> 00:43:20.657
Now you see why I have completely
changed my ideas about you.

736
00:43:20.737 --> 00:43:21.817
You're right.

737
00:43:21.897 --> 00:43:23.677
I was helping the boy out, nothing more.

738
00:43:23.757 --> 00:43:24.757
Of course.

739
00:43:28.497 --> 00:43:31.977
Tell me, where did you leave Pierrot?

740
00:43:32.057 --> 00:43:34.337
Somewhere. I don't quite remember.

741
00:43:36.557 --> 00:43:37.937
Rue de la Beauvoir?

742
00:43:38.157 --> 00:43:39.197
That's it.

743
00:43:39.697 --> 00:43:41.937
You don't mind if I
refresh your memory, do you?

744
00:43:42.017 --> 00:43:44.097
He went to see his poor old mother.

745
00:43:44.177 --> 00:43:45.197
How was she?

746
00:43:45.277 --> 00:43:46.577
I didn't see her.

747
00:43:46.657 --> 00:43:47.737
Why not?

748
00:43:48.317 --> 00:43:49.877
She was in bed. He was sick.

749
00:43:49.957 --> 00:43:51.857
He didn't want to disturb her.

750
00:43:52.177 --> 00:43:54.457
That must have been an
awful shock for Pierre.

751
00:43:54.537 --> 00:43:56.377
He thought she was in France.

752
00:43:56.497 --> 00:43:58.077
I think he got a letter.

753
00:43:58.437 --> 00:43:59.757
Did you see it?

754
00:44:01.857 --> 00:44:04.197
Just a glimpse.

755
00:44:04.517 --> 00:44:08.117
So you left him and you came back alone?

756
00:44:08.197 --> 00:44:10.237
He wanted to stay with her.

757
00:44:10.317 --> 00:44:11.837
That's natural.

758
00:44:13.397 --> 00:44:15.137
Yes, very natural.

759
00:44:15.997 --> 00:44:17.137
Exactly.

760
00:44:17.277 --> 00:44:18.517
Of course.

761
00:44:30.017 --> 00:44:31.437
Want me?

762
00:44:31.777 --> 00:44:33.757
No, we were just talking.

763
00:44:33.837 --> 00:44:34.837
Sit down.

764
00:44:37.917 --> 00:44:40.277
Regis did a fine thing today.

765
00:44:40.357 --> 00:44:43.157
He went down into town with Pierrot.

766
00:44:43.717 --> 00:44:44.857
Fine.

767
00:44:47.137 --> 00:44:49.877
And now you're waiting for poor Pierrot.

768
00:44:49.957 --> 00:44:51.277
Why poor Pierrot?

769
00:44:51.357 --> 00:44:53.257
Because he went down with Regis.

770
00:44:53.337 --> 00:44:54.377
What of it?

771
00:44:54.637 --> 00:44:55.637
Perfect.

772
00:44:55.737 --> 00:44:57.297
Maybe I should say.

773
00:44:57.377 --> 00:45:01.217
And now you're waiting for
Pierrot with poor Regis.

774
00:45:34.477 --> 00:45:35.777
Just relax.

775
00:45:35.857 --> 00:45:37.117
Take it easy.

776
00:45:37.197 --> 00:45:40.097
We understand how
anxious you are about Pio.

777
00:45:40.177 --> 00:45:41.177
Here.

778
00:45:41.317 --> 00:45:42.537
Take this.

779
00:45:46.497 --> 00:45:48.117
Go ahead. Drink.

780
00:45:49.877 --> 00:45:51.937
Don't take a bite out of it.

781
00:45:52.457 --> 00:45:54.137
I don't know what's the matter with me.

782
00:45:54.217 --> 00:45:55.617
You'll get over it.

783
00:45:55.917 --> 00:45:57.976
In an hour you'll feel much better.

784
00:45:58.417 --> 00:45:59.577
Let me go.

785
00:45:59.657 --> 00:46:01.017
Let me go.

786
00:46:01.217 --> 00:46:05.837
With a fever like that, you
mustn't think of exerting yourself.

787
00:46:05.937 --> 00:46:06.937
Cigarette?

788
00:46:07.137 --> 00:46:08.957
Don't make such a fuss.

789
00:46:09.037 --> 00:46:10.457
Go on and smoke.

790
00:46:10.537 --> 00:46:12.477
It'll settle your nerve.

791
00:46:13.097 --> 00:46:17.097
Say, Pepe, his hair is getting
a little long here on his neck.

792
00:46:17.177 --> 00:46:19.706
Don't you think we
ought to cut it for him?

793
00:46:19.837 --> 00:46:21.797
You were fond of Pierre, weren't you?

794
00:46:21.877 --> 00:46:23.717
Oh, I was. I am fond of him.

795
00:46:23.797 --> 00:46:27.277
Well, then, you don't want
to leave before he gets back.

796
00:46:27.357 --> 00:46:30.397
You want to know why he's
been detained, don't you?

797
00:46:30.517 --> 00:46:33.477
Yes, yes. Oh, la, la, la, la.

798
00:46:33.597 --> 00:46:36.197
Oh, master the fever.

799
00:46:36.277 --> 00:46:37.977
I'm worried about you.

800
00:46:38.057 --> 00:46:39.397
He's burning up.

801
00:46:39.477 --> 00:46:42.017
I'm afraid he'll sizzle before long.

802
00:46:44.217 --> 00:46:46.157
I don't know anything about Piero.

803
00:46:46.237 --> 00:46:47.957
Pepe, Pepe, let me go.

804
00:46:48.037 --> 00:46:50.397
You know me. You know him all right.

805
00:46:50.477 --> 00:46:53.237
Tell me you do. Last night I
was the one who came to warn you.

806
00:46:53.317 --> 00:46:55.477
Yes, you were the one. Let me go.

807
00:46:58.697 --> 00:47:00.157
He's delirious.

808
00:47:00.457 --> 00:47:03.477
Charles, he may not last the next round.

809
00:47:04.397 --> 00:47:07.857
How about a little game to
calm him down, all right?

810
00:47:08.557 --> 00:47:10.617
It is really alarming.

811
00:47:10.697 --> 00:47:14.177
If I may say so, he is not at his best.

812
00:47:14.257 --> 00:47:16.297
He must stay right where he is.

813
00:47:16.377 --> 00:47:18.337
We can't be too careful.

814
00:47:24.037 --> 00:47:28.617
What are you doing? Inez, go down to La
Rue de la Beauvoir and see if you can find

815
00:47:28.697 --> 00:47:30.397
out anything about Pierrot.

816
00:47:30.517 --> 00:47:32.577
Try to find him and bring him back, quick.

817
00:47:32.657 --> 00:47:34.197
He went down with Regis.

818
00:47:34.277 --> 00:47:37.497
If you bring him back, Regis may recover.

819
00:47:38.817 --> 00:47:40.077
All right.

820
00:47:45.337 --> 00:47:46.917
Cut him, Regis.

821
00:47:56.337 --> 00:47:58.137
The black spot.

822
00:47:58.997 --> 00:48:01.057
Oh, that's bad.

823
00:48:06.757 --> 00:48:08.697
I suppose you can't find him.

824
00:48:08.777 --> 00:48:09.877
Don't worry.

825
00:48:20.297 --> 00:48:21.617
This way.

826
00:48:27.637 --> 00:48:29.317
Women look so mysterious.

827
00:48:29.397 --> 00:48:31.737
No doubt they say the same about you.

828
00:48:44.437 --> 00:48:45.457
Tramp?

829
00:48:45.597 --> 00:48:47.317
Put you good at heart.

830
00:48:47.697 --> 00:48:48.717
What's the matter with me?

831
00:48:48.797 --> 00:48:51.757
I'm not myself. What
kind of a game is this?

832
00:48:51.897 --> 00:48:54.057
Concentrate! He's thinking of Pierrot.

833
00:48:54.137 --> 00:48:58.297
Yes, of course. Worry over a friend can
cause unutterable anguish to a sensitive

834
00:48:58.377 --> 00:48:59.037
nature.

835
00:48:59.117 --> 00:49:00.737
You mean it makes him sweat?

836
00:49:00.817 --> 00:49:05.037
A certain exudation hyperactuated
by an emotional stimulation.

837
00:49:05.117 --> 00:49:06.617
You don't mean him.

838
00:49:06.697 --> 00:49:07.857
Uh, tell me out.

839
00:49:07.937 --> 00:49:11.761
Take care, Regis. Never go back
on a friend when he's in trouble.

840
00:49:12.617 --> 00:49:14.417
Still waiting, little woman?

841
00:49:46.797 --> 00:49:47.797
Oh,

842
00:49:48.277 --> 00:49:49.717
you know what this reminds me of?

843
00:49:49.797 --> 00:49:52.057
A little place in New York on 42nd Street.

844
00:49:52.137 --> 00:49:54.078
That's the thing about traveling.

845
00:49:55.157 --> 00:49:58.397
One time I was in Corsica
and I thought I was in Turkey.

846
00:49:58.477 --> 00:50:02.595
And remember the time we were on
the Nile and I thought it was Venice?

847
00:50:03.497 --> 00:50:06.897
Tell me, do they have native music here?

848
00:50:06.977 --> 00:50:08.277
On the photograph.

849
00:50:08.357 --> 00:50:09.997
Oh, well.

850
00:50:25.417 --> 00:50:28.357
What's that one? It's a checker tepper.

851
00:50:28.437 --> 00:50:29.937
Never heard of it.

852
00:50:30.237 --> 00:50:31.797
Must be native music.

853
00:50:31.877 --> 00:50:32.877
Mm-hmm.

854
00:50:35.797 --> 00:50:39.503
So you wanted to take another
look at this strange wild animal?

855
00:50:39.897 --> 00:50:42.597
Strange, but not so very wild.

856
00:50:42.917 --> 00:50:44.537
How do you like my cage?

857
00:50:44.617 --> 00:50:46.697
I don't know yet.

858
00:50:47.217 --> 00:50:49.797
Do you like Algiers?
I don't like traveling.

859
00:50:49.877 --> 00:50:50.937
It makes me home-see.

860
00:50:51.017 --> 00:50:51.657
Does it?

861
00:50:51.737 --> 00:50:54.877
I can't see Paris when I
open my eyes in the morning.

862
00:50:54.957 --> 00:50:56.898
I want to go right back to sleep.

863
00:50:57.157 --> 00:50:59.217
Do you know Paris?

864
00:51:01.197 --> 00:51:03.077
Do I know Paris?

865
00:51:34.377 --> 00:51:36.257
Cigarette? Thanks.

866
00:51:38.817 --> 00:51:40.257
Is there a light?

867
00:51:43.197 --> 00:51:45.557
We're a long way from home.

868
00:51:48.937 --> 00:51:50.317
Excuse me.

869
00:51:55.837 --> 00:51:59.637
Well, he still thinks
he's playing his last card.

870
00:52:01.377 --> 00:52:02.637
I'll tell her you said so.

871
00:52:02.717 --> 00:52:05.037
No, no, no. I mean the rock she's wearing.

872
00:52:05.117 --> 00:52:09.037
Now, if it was me, I'd get them first
and then do the fancy stuff afterwards.

873
00:52:09.117 --> 00:52:09.797
Shut up.

874
00:52:09.877 --> 00:52:11.557
You can't talk to me like that.

875
00:52:11.637 --> 00:52:13.377
You heard me. Shut up.

876
00:52:16.557 --> 00:52:17.557
Okay.

877
00:52:20.657 --> 00:52:22.237
He was talking about me?

878
00:52:22.317 --> 00:52:23.697
He was worried about you.

879
00:52:23.777 --> 00:52:24.697
About me?

880
00:52:24.777 --> 00:52:26.477
Well, that stabbed your arm.

881
00:52:26.617 --> 00:52:29.057
Oh, that's nice of him.

882
00:52:29.137 --> 00:52:30.177
Not worrying yourself?

883
00:52:30.257 --> 00:52:31.377
No.

884
00:52:31.657 --> 00:52:33.617
Not while I'm with you.

885
00:52:35.657 --> 00:52:36.797
Right.

886
00:52:38.697 --> 00:52:40.097
This is something.

887
00:52:40.177 --> 00:52:40.897
Isn't it?

888
00:52:40.977 --> 00:52:43.317
And it hardly weighs anything.

889
00:52:43.437 --> 00:52:44.437
Look.

890
00:52:45.297 --> 00:52:48.417
At least 20,000 francs, hmm?

891
00:52:48.717 --> 00:52:49.657
E de zero.

892
00:52:49.737 --> 00:52:52.497
Oh, I mean, what I would get for it.

893
00:52:53.877 --> 00:52:56.617
Here, put it on again.

894
00:52:57.457 --> 00:52:59.237
You put it on.

895
00:53:33.257 --> 00:53:34.817
Want a dance?

896
00:53:34.897 --> 00:53:36.097
Yes.

897
00:53:59.757 --> 00:54:01.057
What's your name?

898
00:54:01.137 --> 00:54:03.077
Gabrielle. They call me Gabi.

899
00:54:03.157 --> 00:54:03.977
Married?

900
00:54:04.057 --> 00:54:05.077
No.

901
00:54:05.157 --> 00:54:06.517
Widow? No.

902
00:54:06.597 --> 00:54:07.597
Why not?

903
00:54:07.837 --> 00:54:10.037
Who are you with? My fiancée.

904
00:54:10.117 --> 00:54:11.877
What is he like? Jealous.

905
00:54:11.957 --> 00:54:12.857
Oh.

906
00:54:12.937 --> 00:54:15.277
Stopping at the hotel? I let it.

907
00:54:16.877 --> 00:54:18.657
What are you laughing at?

908
00:54:18.737 --> 00:54:19.697
Nothing.

909
00:54:19.777 --> 00:54:20.617
Too bad.

910
00:54:20.697 --> 00:54:21.497
Too bad?

911
00:54:21.577 --> 00:54:23.277
Too bad I don't know you better.

912
00:54:23.357 --> 00:54:23.997
Why?

913
00:54:24.077 --> 00:54:26.037
Because I would slap your face.

914
00:54:26.117 --> 00:54:29.097
When people laugh around
me, I like to know why.

915
00:54:35.297 --> 00:54:38.197
This all reminds me when I was a kid.

916
00:54:38.437 --> 00:54:42.497
We used to dance in the
streets on holidays, New Year's,

917
00:54:42.577 --> 00:54:44.977
1st of May. 14th of July.

918
00:54:45.197 --> 00:54:48.117
How do you know? What
do you think I was doing?

919
00:54:48.277 --> 00:54:50.557
Too bad you weren't in my neighborhood.

920
00:54:50.637 --> 00:54:52.437
Breu de la Boyere. Breu de la Boyere?

921
00:54:52.517 --> 00:54:55.458
That's where I live.
I went to school on the hill.

922
00:54:56.117 --> 00:54:58.097
It's next door to me. No.

923
00:55:07.537 --> 00:55:08.997
Let's go out.

924
00:55:09.317 --> 00:55:10.377
Where to?

925
00:55:10.457 --> 00:55:11.657
To the terrace.

926
00:55:14.897 --> 00:55:16.337
Can you see the Harvard?

927
00:55:16.417 --> 00:55:17.557
You can see Montmartre.

928
00:55:17.637 --> 00:55:18.977
And the Champs-Élysées?

929
00:55:19.057 --> 00:55:20.597
And the Place Blanche.

930
00:55:20.677 --> 00:55:22.997
I love the Place Blanche.

931
00:55:23.537 --> 00:55:25.197
Oh, I can't.

932
00:55:26.117 --> 00:55:27.117
I'm friends.

933
00:55:29.897 --> 00:55:31.557
But I'll come back.

934
00:55:31.637 --> 00:55:34.017
When? As soon as I can.

935
00:55:34.097 --> 00:55:35.097
When?

936
00:55:36.017 --> 00:55:37.177
Tomorrow.

937
00:55:37.827 --> 00:55:39.317
How can I be sure?

938
00:55:39.927 --> 00:55:41.697
I'll never break a promise.

939
00:55:45.017 --> 00:55:46.557
Let me go.

940
00:55:47.037 --> 00:55:48.637
Why should I?

941
00:55:49.117 --> 00:55:50.877
Because I'll ask you.

942
00:55:52.097 --> 00:55:53.377
Say please.

943
00:55:55.077 --> 00:55:56.597
You're rude.

944
00:55:57.857 --> 00:55:59.057
Am I?

945
00:56:07.237 --> 00:56:09.057
I'll be expecting you.

946
00:56:09.437 --> 00:56:10.457
Here.

947
00:56:10.857 --> 00:56:14.117
It would be nice if we could
meet at the Place Bloch.

948
00:56:23.977 --> 00:56:25.757
Well, what about Pierrot?

949
00:56:25.837 --> 00:56:27.337
I don't know.

950
00:56:27.617 --> 00:56:29.117
Didn't you go down to find him?

951
00:56:29.197 --> 00:56:31.337
I didn't want to leave you alone.

952
00:56:31.417 --> 00:56:33.241
I'm not alone. I'm with Madame.

953
00:56:33.457 --> 00:56:34.797
Do as I told you.

954
00:56:39.257 --> 00:56:40.257
Pierrot!

955
00:56:41.737 --> 00:56:43.237
Where is he? Who?

956
00:56:43.317 --> 00:56:45.117
Regis. Where is he?

957
00:56:45.917 --> 00:56:47.017
Come on.

958
00:56:47.397 --> 00:56:48.877
They got me, Pepe.

959
00:56:48.957 --> 00:56:49.997
The police.

960
00:56:50.077 --> 00:56:51.977
I didn't listen to you.

961
00:56:59.057 --> 00:57:00.457
Thank you.

962
00:57:53.877 --> 00:57:55.997
No!

963
00:57:56.417 --> 00:57:57.577
No!

964
00:57:57.697 --> 00:57:59.157
No!

965
00:59:26.017 --> 00:59:27.117
Pierrot.

966
00:59:28.277 --> 00:59:29.997
There is no sense to it.

967
00:59:30.077 --> 00:59:31.877
That's what they said.

968
00:59:32.017 --> 00:59:32.977
They?

969
00:59:33.057 --> 00:59:35.257
Those people. They were frightened.

970
00:59:35.337 --> 00:59:37.297
They said they'd never come back.

971
00:59:47.717 --> 00:59:49.797
I was fond of Pierrot.

972
00:59:49.877 --> 00:59:52.437
I regarded him almost as his son.

973
00:59:54.777 --> 00:59:58.037
Pepe, there's no use in
thinking about Pierrot.

974
00:59:58.117 --> 01:00:00.117
Don't you tell me what you think.

975
01:00:02.637 --> 01:00:04.337
It is a sad thing.

976
01:00:04.417 --> 01:00:07.137
Have you finished? I beg your pardon.

977
01:00:07.217 --> 01:00:09.037
It's very sad. You have fun of him.

978
01:00:09.117 --> 01:00:09.997
That's enough.

979
01:00:10.077 --> 01:00:11.757
Can't a man talk.

980
01:00:40.957 --> 01:00:44.957
Well? Well, it's finished.

981
01:00:45.357 --> 01:00:46.877
Well, it's finished.

982
01:00:54.437 --> 01:00:57.217
I did everything you
would have done, Pepe.

983
01:00:57.877 --> 01:01:00.297
I was all alone at the cemetery.

984
01:01:00.377 --> 01:01:05.037
I followed the custom of your people,
a handful of earth from the body,

985
01:01:05.117 --> 01:01:09.797
and flowers to make him feel
at home in such a strange place.

986
01:01:14.077 --> 01:01:18.497
It's hard not to be able to go down to
say goodbye to your friend on his last

987
01:01:18.577 --> 01:01:19.577
journey.

988
01:01:55.217 --> 01:01:56.777
I'm your friend, Pepe.

989
01:01:56.857 --> 01:01:58.577
I know how you feel.

990
01:01:58.657 --> 01:02:00.877
You're a prisoner in the Casper.

991
01:02:00.957 --> 01:02:04.697
But the day will come when they
won't be able to prevent your leaving.

992
01:02:04.777 --> 01:02:07.677
You'll go out of the
Casper in spite of the moor.

993
01:02:07.757 --> 01:02:09.437
I'll get out whenever I wish.

994
01:02:09.517 --> 01:02:12.797
When you go, you'll go quietly,
the way Pierrot went.

995
01:02:12.877 --> 01:02:14.237
Feet first.

996
01:02:14.317 --> 01:02:15.817
Be patient.

997
01:02:15.897 --> 01:02:20.297
When the time comes, they'll take
off their hats and let you pass.

998
01:02:20.377 --> 01:02:21.917
I'll go out alive.

999
01:02:24.877 --> 01:02:27.437
I don't think you're as foolish as that.

1000
01:02:33.557 --> 01:02:34.757
Come down!

1001
01:02:34.977 --> 01:02:36.117
I've heard enough!

1002
01:02:40.357 --> 01:02:42.557
Music, singing, gibberish.

1003
01:02:42.637 --> 01:02:44.257
I'm sorry for you.

1004
01:02:45.177 --> 01:02:46.857
How is she? She?

1005
01:02:46.937 --> 01:02:49.237
You know. I'm afraid
you won't see her again.

1006
01:02:49.317 --> 01:02:51.277
The last visit was a
little too much for her.

1007
01:02:51.357 --> 01:02:53.657
She got a bad impression of the Caspar.

1008
01:02:54.877 --> 01:02:56.197
Why should it be a pity?

1009
01:02:56.277 --> 01:02:59.117
For your sake, since it
seems to mean so much to you.

1010
01:02:59.197 --> 01:03:00.197
To me?

1011
01:03:00.297 --> 01:03:03.097
So that's what you're so sorry about.

1012
01:03:03.177 --> 01:03:06.217
Why are you standing there, staring at me?

1013
01:03:06.297 --> 01:03:07.497
Do as I told you.

1014
01:03:07.577 --> 01:03:08.597
Go along.

1015
01:03:09.597 --> 01:03:10.757
And you too.

1016
01:03:10.837 --> 01:03:11.917
Get out.

1017
01:03:12.597 --> 01:03:13.937
I've heard enough.

1018
01:03:14.337 --> 01:03:15.277
And you.

1019
01:03:15.357 --> 01:03:17.597
I'm sick of looking at you.

1020
01:03:20.337 --> 01:03:22.737
You seem to be sick of everything.

1021
01:03:23.077 --> 01:03:24.077
Right.

1022
01:03:24.877 --> 01:03:27.577
to see you again if it could
possibly, but there's no chance.

1023
01:03:27.657 --> 01:03:30.377
So, she's not coming back.

1024
01:03:30.637 --> 01:03:31.657
That's fine.

1025
01:03:31.737 --> 01:03:33.757
What? All that swell jewelry.

1026
01:03:33.837 --> 01:03:35.397
You had it right in the palm of your hand.

1027
01:03:35.477 --> 01:03:36.257
That's enough.

1028
01:03:36.337 --> 01:03:39.197
These people who look as if
they can tear down everything.

1029
01:03:39.277 --> 01:03:42.117
And when a woman looks at them,
they get as soft as butter.

1030
01:03:42.197 --> 01:03:44.097
Get out. Well, I'm not made of butter.

1031
01:03:44.177 --> 01:03:46.337
Not me. Get out. OK.

1032
01:03:46.977 --> 01:03:49.617
Your friends have no tax, my dear Pepe.

1033
01:03:49.697 --> 01:03:51.997
They have no respect for
the beauty of your anguish.

1034
01:03:52.077 --> 01:03:55.737
Oh. I know how it pains you
to live among this cattle.

1035
01:03:55.817 --> 01:03:58.437
Let me assure you.
They can't keep me here.

1036
01:03:58.777 --> 01:03:59.937
I'm free.

1037
01:04:00.017 --> 01:04:01.197
Free to go.

1038
01:04:01.277 --> 01:04:02.837
I'm sick of it.

1039
01:04:03.137 --> 01:04:04.157
All of you.

1040
01:04:04.237 --> 01:04:06.417
I'm sick of listening to you.

1041
01:04:06.497 --> 01:04:08.477
And I'm sick of looking at you.

1042
01:04:08.557 --> 01:04:10.437
I cannot put a feel like it.

1043
01:04:10.517 --> 01:04:11.857
None of you can stop me.

1044
01:04:11.937 --> 01:04:14.497
Oh, listen to me, Pepe.
I don't need your advice.

1045
01:04:14.577 --> 01:04:15.757
None of you.

1046
01:04:15.837 --> 01:04:17.337
I'm free to do as I please.

1047
01:04:17.417 --> 01:04:18.757
Prey! You hear that?

1048
01:04:18.837 --> 01:04:20.037
You're walking into a trap.

1049
01:04:20.117 --> 01:04:22.257
You know better. They can't touch me.

1050
01:04:22.337 --> 01:04:23.997
I'm going down. Get out of the way.

1051
01:04:24.077 --> 01:04:24.617
Act me.

1052
01:04:24.697 --> 01:04:26.097
And what I please is now.

1053
01:04:26.177 --> 01:04:27.597
Get out of my way.

1054
01:04:36.237 --> 01:04:38.497
He's got mad. He's going down to the town.

1055
01:04:38.577 --> 01:04:39.697
He won't listen.

1056
01:04:59.257 --> 01:05:00.257
Hello?

1057
01:05:06.137 --> 01:05:08.197
Go. I'll attend to it.

1058
01:05:08.717 --> 01:05:10.037
Inspector's remain.

1059
01:05:10.117 --> 01:05:12.277
He says Pepe Lamoco's coming out.

1060
01:05:31.057 --> 01:05:32.957
Herbert, Herbert, don't go.

1061
01:05:33.037 --> 01:05:34.217
You're mad.

1062
01:05:39.537 --> 01:05:41.717
Herbert, don't go. Please don't go.

1063
01:05:41.797 --> 01:05:45.017
I didn't want to tell you
this, but she's up there now.

1064
01:05:45.097 --> 01:05:47.377
At your own house, waiting for you.

1065
01:06:03.197 --> 01:06:04.377
Where is she?

1066
01:06:08.097 --> 01:06:09.297
Where is she?

1067
01:06:09.657 --> 01:06:11.357
You lied to me, didn't you?

1068
01:06:11.437 --> 01:06:12.997
Answer me, didn't you?

1069
01:06:14.257 --> 01:06:17.277
It was the only way I
could keep you from going.

1070
01:06:17.637 --> 01:06:22.337
If I had asked you not to go for me,
you wouldn't have listened to me.

1071
01:06:25.457 --> 01:06:26.457
So...

1072
01:06:31.217 --> 01:06:33.937
You ought to be fed up
with a fellow like me.

1073
01:06:37.617 --> 01:06:40.499
I didn't know I could
make such a fool of myself.

1074
01:06:45.577 --> 01:06:48.117
You deserve something better than this.

1075
01:06:48.197 --> 01:06:50.297
It's not what you deserve.

1076
01:06:51.977 --> 01:06:53.757
It's what you want.

1077
01:06:54.637 --> 01:06:56.637
Why do you worry about me?

1078
01:06:56.717 --> 01:06:57.777
It's no good.

1079
01:06:57.857 --> 01:07:01.437
I have a charm that brings me luck.

1080
01:07:03.017 --> 01:07:05.697
You got to spot luck this time.

1081
01:07:05.777 --> 01:07:07.677
All the while I was running.

1082
01:07:07.757 --> 01:07:09.997
I kept my hands so...

1083
01:07:10.137 --> 01:07:11.837
But you caught me.

1084
01:07:12.137 --> 01:07:14.837
I didn't know you could run so far.

1085
01:07:14.957 --> 01:07:17.137
Don't forget I've had practice.

1086
01:07:17.397 --> 01:07:19.338
But nobody ever caught me before.

1087
01:07:20.817 --> 01:07:23.097
Next time, give me a head start.

1088
01:07:24.217 --> 01:07:25.657
Next time?

1089
01:07:27.437 --> 01:07:28.837
Don't worry.

1090
01:07:28.997 --> 01:07:30.717
Not till I get my breath.

1091
01:07:33.457 --> 01:07:34.857
I'm thirsty.

1092
01:07:34.937 --> 01:07:36.257
I'll get it.

1093
01:07:37.917 --> 01:07:39.697
No, you won't.

1094
01:08:23.137 --> 01:08:24.557
Here I am.

1095
01:08:24.637 --> 01:08:26.557
I said I'd be here.

1096
01:08:27.037 --> 01:08:28.057
Well,

1097
01:08:28.277 --> 01:08:30.512
you look as though you'd seen a ghost.

1098
01:08:38.577 --> 01:08:41.437
Thank you.

1099
01:09:39.577 --> 01:09:40.937
You're beautiful.

1100
01:09:41.577 --> 01:09:42.957
That's easy to say.

1101
01:09:43.037 --> 01:09:45.237
I know a lot of people have told you.

1102
01:09:45.317 --> 01:09:47.846
But what I'm telling
you is different, see?

1103
01:09:48.397 --> 01:09:50.317
For me, you're more than that.

1104
01:09:50.397 --> 01:09:52.237
For two years, I've been lost.

1105
01:09:52.317 --> 01:09:54.357
Like walking in my sleep.

1106
01:09:54.437 --> 01:09:56.477
Suddenly, I wake up. That's you.

1107
01:09:56.657 --> 01:10:01.017
I don't know what I've been doing all that
time, waiting for you without knowing it.

1108
01:10:01.097 --> 01:10:02.921
Do you know what you are to me?

1109
01:10:03.897 --> 01:10:04.817
Paris.

1110
01:10:04.897 --> 01:10:05.997
That's you.

1111
01:10:06.097 --> 01:10:07.097
Paris.

1112
01:10:07.437 --> 01:10:08.837
With you, I escape.

1113
01:10:08.917 --> 01:10:09.877
Follow me?

1114
01:10:09.957 --> 01:10:11.177
The whole town.

1115
01:10:11.257 --> 01:10:13.377
A spring morning in Paris.

1116
01:10:14.177 --> 01:10:15.597
You're lovely.

1117
01:10:16.357 --> 01:10:17.797
You're marvelous.

1118
01:10:18.597 --> 01:10:21.237
And you know what you remind me of?

1119
01:10:22.537 --> 01:10:24.157
The subway.

1120
01:10:29.277 --> 01:10:31.077
Close your eyes.

1121
01:10:33.757 --> 01:10:34.997
Listen.

1122
01:10:36.537 --> 01:10:38.337
Can you hear it?

1123
01:10:38.617 --> 01:10:40.777
That's my heart beating.

1124
01:10:41.157 --> 01:10:43.357
Does it go like a subway train?

1125
01:10:43.477 --> 01:10:44.477
Faster.

1126
01:10:45.687 --> 01:10:48.967
You're all silk and you
jingle when you walk.

1127
01:10:49.047 --> 01:10:51.867
And with all that shishy,
you make me think of the subway.

1128
01:10:51.947 --> 01:10:52.887
Isn't that funny?

1129
01:10:52.967 --> 01:10:56.227
And potato chips and
coffee on the boulevard.

1130
01:11:00.487 --> 01:11:02.347
What did you do before?

1131
01:11:02.527 --> 01:11:03.847
Get all wood.

1132
01:11:04.767 --> 01:11:06.267
Before the jewels?

1133
01:11:06.447 --> 01:11:08.247
I wanted them.

1134
01:11:20.387 --> 01:11:22.767
It's late. I must go.

1135
01:11:25.807 --> 01:11:27.747
Because you don't come tomorrow?

1136
01:11:30.407 --> 01:11:32.167
Suppose I don't.

1137
01:11:32.427 --> 01:11:35.207
Can't you ever get away from the Casper?

1138
01:11:35.287 --> 01:11:37.207
Why do you ask? Can't you?

1139
01:11:37.287 --> 01:11:37.967
No.

1140
01:11:38.047 --> 01:11:39.327
I'm caught here.

1141
01:11:39.407 --> 01:11:41.127
Like a bear in a hole.

1142
01:11:41.207 --> 01:11:43.607
Dogs barking, hunters all around.

1143
01:11:45.447 --> 01:11:46.867
You like that?

1144
01:11:55.507 --> 01:11:57.227
Maybe it's lucky for you.

1145
01:11:58.347 --> 01:12:01.087
I don't like it. And it's not lucky.

1146
01:12:01.627 --> 01:12:02.767
You're right.

1147
01:12:03.347 --> 01:12:05.507
If you don't come back,
I might do anything.

1148
01:12:05.587 --> 01:12:07.967
I might go down to the hotel to get you.

1149
01:12:08.827 --> 01:12:10.187
Tomorrow, Pepe.

1150
01:12:10.367 --> 01:12:13.967
Tomorrow? I'll never break a promise.

1151
01:12:33.787 --> 01:12:35.827
You smell good.

1152
01:12:36.707 --> 01:12:38.647
The subway?

1153
01:12:38.947 --> 01:12:40.407
Streamline.

1154
01:13:30.107 --> 01:13:32.747
Hey, enter!

1155
01:13:34.467 --> 01:13:37.827
Tomorrow, five o'clock.

1156
01:13:39.207 --> 01:13:41.560
Take Mademoiselle Bourgeois-Marin Gault.

1157
01:13:55.727 --> 01:13:57.167
Did you get them?

1158
01:13:57.407 --> 01:13:58.207
What?

1159
01:13:58.287 --> 01:13:59.527
The hard way.

1160
01:14:00.827 --> 01:14:02.307
What's the matter with you?

1161
01:14:02.387 --> 01:14:04.967
If you didn't get the jewels, you
said they've been wasting your time.

1162
01:14:05.047 --> 01:14:06.607
What were you doing in there?

1163
01:14:06.687 --> 01:14:07.427
Where?

1164
01:14:07.507 --> 01:14:08.507
There.

1165
01:14:08.687 --> 01:14:10.207
You're mistaken.

1166
01:14:10.527 --> 01:14:11.987
You were not there.

1167
01:14:12.387 --> 01:14:13.907
Say that again.

1168
01:14:15.507 --> 01:14:17.107
We were in pace.

1169
01:14:17.187 --> 01:14:18.187
What?

1170
01:14:20.647 --> 01:14:21.687
Okay.

1171
01:14:43.207 --> 01:14:47.927
Life is simple if you try to enjoy before
you die every bit of happiness along the

1172
01:14:48.007 --> 01:14:48.587
way.

1173
01:14:48.667 --> 01:14:50.027
Take the joy that comes to you.

1174
01:14:50.107 --> 01:14:53.727
Suddenly the world is new with a
song that keeps you dancing every day.

1175
01:14:53.807 --> 01:14:55.367
C'est la vie.

1176
01:14:55.887 --> 01:14:58.167
Fall in love and life is honey.

1177
01:14:58.547 --> 01:15:00.807
That's life, you don't need money.

1178
01:15:01.167 --> 01:15:04.507
If you've got a little honey in your arms.

1179
01:15:04.587 --> 01:15:05.667
C'est la vie.

1180
01:15:06.447 --> 01:15:08.807
I'm in heaven and I know it.

1181
01:15:09.047 --> 01:15:11.567
Can I help it if I show it?

1182
01:15:11.787 --> 01:15:14.887
Life is sweet as sweet can be for me.

1183
01:15:14.967 --> 01:15:17.807
The love is very necessary.

1184
01:15:18.307 --> 01:15:20.427
You'll be happy, c'est la vie.

1185
01:15:20.507 --> 01:15:23.607
You don't know just what you
miss if you live without a kiss.

1186
01:15:23.687 --> 01:15:26.275
For a kiss can bring
you winter into spring.

1187
01:15:26.547 --> 01:15:29.767
Everybody will agree, if you fall
in love like me, you'll be happy,

1188
01:15:29.847 --> 01:15:31.407
you will laugh and you will sing.

1189
01:15:31.487 --> 01:15:32.987
C'est la vie.

1190
01:15:33.707 --> 01:15:35.827
That's the life we should be living.

1191
01:15:36.567 --> 01:15:38.827
Kisses, morning, dawn and evening.

1192
01:15:39.027 --> 01:15:41.047
That's the life that I've been living.

1193
01:15:41.127 --> 01:15:42.287
C'est l'amour.

1194
01:15:42.367 --> 01:15:43.607
C'est la vie.

1195
01:15:44.447 --> 01:15:46.907
There is nothing like that feeling.

1196
01:15:49.547 --> 01:15:53.067
than the feeling you're in love may with.

1197
01:15:53.147 --> 01:15:55.967
Love is very necessary.

1198
01:15:56.127 --> 01:15:58.527
Fall in love and you'll
be happy, c'est la vie.

1199
01:15:58.607 --> 01:16:01.207
Love is very necessary.

1200
01:16:01.547 --> 01:16:03.887
Fall in love and you'll
be happy, c'est la vie.

1201
01:16:03.967 --> 01:16:05.827
How? What happened?

1202
01:16:05.907 --> 01:16:06.767
Don't you know?

1203
01:16:06.847 --> 01:16:08.207
It's a holiday.

1204
01:16:08.287 --> 01:16:09.727
No, I didn't know what the is.

1205
01:16:09.807 --> 01:16:11.987
It's Sunday. Everyone takes a holiday.

1206
01:16:12.067 --> 01:16:14.887
But it's Sunday. If I say so, it's Sunday.

1207
01:16:14.967 --> 01:16:18.967
It's Sunday. As the travel with you,
you always think it's Thursday.

1208
01:16:19.107 --> 01:16:21.487
I didn't think so yesterday.

1209
01:16:21.907 --> 01:16:24.347
Just as a favor to me, let it be Sunday.

1210
01:16:24.427 --> 01:16:26.587
I want to stroll on the boulevards.

1211
01:16:28.527 --> 01:16:31.107
I have a date at the Place Blanche.

1212
01:16:38.847 --> 01:16:40.347
Hello, everybody.

1213
01:16:40.507 --> 01:16:42.047
How do you like my singing?

1214
01:16:42.127 --> 01:16:43.707
What's that good of it?

1215
01:16:44.367 --> 01:16:47.067
You ought to appreciate
the finer things of life.

1216
01:16:47.147 --> 01:16:48.367
Who? Him?

1217
01:16:48.447 --> 01:16:49.447
Now,

1218
01:16:49.667 --> 01:16:51.367
when you feel like that, sing.

1219
01:16:51.447 --> 01:16:53.247
It quietes the nerves.

1220
01:16:54.187 --> 01:16:55.587
You seem pleased.

1221
01:16:55.667 --> 01:16:56.987
You've seen her again.

1222
01:16:57.067 --> 01:16:58.087
Wouldn't you like to know?

1223
01:16:58.167 --> 01:17:00.107
Oh, well, if you don't
want to confide in me.

1224
01:17:00.187 --> 01:17:02.847
Well, our inspector got himself a haircut.

1225
01:17:02.927 --> 01:17:04.987
Did she come back? A regular Romeo.

1226
01:17:05.067 --> 01:17:06.367
You ought to get a permanent wave.

1227
01:17:06.447 --> 01:17:07.867
You're expecting it again today?

1228
01:17:07.947 --> 01:17:10.967
The trouble with you, inspector,
is that you do too much inspecting.

1229
01:17:11.047 --> 01:17:13.647
Now, not a word about
what I have told you.

1230
01:17:13.727 --> 01:17:15.527
It's just between ourselves.

1231
01:17:16.047 --> 01:17:17.047
Here?

1232
01:17:46.027 --> 01:17:47.087
Inspector.

1233
01:17:47.167 --> 01:17:48.627
Good afternoon.

1234
01:17:48.867 --> 01:17:51.167
I was puzzled when you phoned.

1235
01:17:51.247 --> 01:17:55.787
My mission is a rather
delicate one, but necessary.

1236
01:17:56.487 --> 01:18:02.147
I merely wish to suggest that your
fiancé is a little too fond of,

1237
01:18:02.907 --> 01:18:06.627
shall we say, the local
color of the Casper.

1238
01:18:07.467 --> 01:18:09.287
What is all this?

1239
01:18:09.467 --> 01:18:12.027
The Casper's heart is a little too fond
of, She's hardly the place for a woman

1240
01:18:12.107 --> 01:18:12.747
alone.

1241
01:18:12.827 --> 01:18:16.807
She attracts too much attention,
excites too much desire.

1242
01:18:17.127 --> 01:18:21.247
We naturally wish to protect
her from any embarrassment.

1243
01:18:21.927 --> 01:18:25.347
Further embarrassment can
very easily be avoided.

1244
01:18:25.547 --> 01:18:29.107
She must not return to the Casper.

1245
01:18:35.447 --> 01:18:36.887
Come in.

1246
01:18:39.807 --> 01:18:41.527
Sorry to disturb you.

1247
01:18:43.447 --> 01:18:45.607
You're going out? Looks that way.

1248
01:18:45.687 --> 01:18:46.667
Where are you going?

1249
01:18:46.747 --> 01:18:47.707
A walk.

1250
01:18:47.787 --> 01:18:48.787
But where?

1251
01:18:48.907 --> 01:18:50.427
In the Champs Elysees.

1252
01:18:50.587 --> 01:18:52.727
May I ask you to give
me a sensible answer?

1253
01:18:52.807 --> 01:18:54.487
Then ask me a sensible question.

1254
01:18:54.567 --> 01:18:55.887
Where could I go?

1255
01:18:55.967 --> 01:18:58.407
I don't know anyone in Algiers.

1256
01:18:58.727 --> 01:19:00.387
I just walked straight ahead.

1257
01:19:00.467 --> 01:19:01.767
Straight ahead?

1258
01:19:01.847 --> 01:19:03.387
And where does that take you?

1259
01:19:03.467 --> 01:19:05.287
I'll know when I get there.

1260
01:19:06.387 --> 01:19:08.847
Because you're not going.
Oh, yes, my dear.

1261
01:19:08.927 --> 01:19:10.367
Your hotel woes me.

1262
01:19:10.447 --> 01:19:12.607
The head waiter looks like an undertaker.

1263
01:19:12.687 --> 01:19:17.387
And every time I step into this apartment,
it looks more like a funeral parlor.

1264
01:19:17.467 --> 01:19:18.607
Goodbye, darling.

1265
01:19:20.527 --> 01:19:22.087
I know where you're going.

1266
01:19:22.167 --> 01:19:24.027
Huh? You're going to the Caspar.

1267
01:19:24.107 --> 01:19:25.907
So? You go there every day.

1268
01:19:25.987 --> 01:19:28.067
Do I? To meet Pepe Lamoco.

1269
01:19:28.487 --> 01:19:29.487
Ah.

1270
01:19:30.207 --> 01:19:32.547
So now you're spying on me.

1271
01:19:34.047 --> 01:19:35.827
You're going to be my wife.

1272
01:19:37.327 --> 01:19:39.507
And I won't allow you to behave like this.

1273
01:19:39.587 --> 01:19:40.987
I'm glad you told me.

1274
01:19:41.067 --> 01:19:42.187
What do you mean?

1275
01:19:43.867 --> 01:19:45.607
We've got to be honest.

1276
01:19:45.707 --> 01:19:47.627
Why do you think I'm marrying you?

1277
01:19:47.707 --> 01:19:49.647
Look at yourself and then look at me.

1278
01:19:49.727 --> 01:19:51.207
I've never lied to you.

1279
01:19:51.287 --> 01:19:53.747
You knew I didn't love you
when I promised to marry you,

1280
01:19:53.827 --> 01:19:55.487
and you thought it was all right.

1281
01:19:55.567 --> 01:19:57.887
Until we're married, I do as I please.

1282
01:19:57.967 --> 01:19:59.307
That's fair enough.

1283
01:19:59.487 --> 01:20:01.227
I forbid you to go.

1284
01:20:01.567 --> 01:20:03.007
It's a waste of time.

1285
01:20:03.087 --> 01:20:06.263
If you go now, there'll be
no use in your coming back.

1286
01:20:06.387 --> 01:20:08.947
You thought it all out
pretty clearly, haven't you?

1287
01:20:09.027 --> 01:20:11.467
And I advise you to do the same.

1288
01:20:11.727 --> 01:20:12.787
All right.

1289
01:20:12.947 --> 01:20:13.947
Goodbye.

1290
01:20:14.867 --> 01:20:16.567
Do it, Camille. Don't.

1291
01:20:20.627 --> 01:20:21.627
No.

1292
01:20:21.947 --> 01:20:24.247
What? You can't go to the Casper.

1293
01:20:24.327 --> 01:20:27.287
But really? Your fiancé
was trying to spare you.

1294
01:20:27.367 --> 01:20:30.087
He didn't want to tell you
the truth as I told the time.

1295
01:20:30.167 --> 01:20:33.827
An attempt was made to capture
Pepelemocle this afternoon.

1296
01:20:33.927 --> 01:20:35.707
In a sense, it was successful.

1297
01:20:36.387 --> 01:20:37.707
Not alive.

1298
01:20:37.787 --> 01:20:39.307
He was killed.

1299
01:21:26.767 --> 01:21:29.967
I just came to tell you it's Thursday.

1300
01:21:30.747 --> 01:21:32.067
I know.

1301
01:21:32.607 --> 01:21:35.087
I was right all the time.

1302
01:21:38.707 --> 01:21:41.587
So this is the Place Blanche.

1303
01:21:42.807 --> 01:21:45.197
It's not much fun on Thursdays.

1304
01:21:45.367 --> 01:21:47.667
It doesn't seem like Paris.

1305
01:22:01.087 --> 01:22:02.987
What's got into him?

1306
01:22:03.607 --> 01:22:06.367
Weren't you ever disappointed in love?

1307
01:22:08.347 --> 01:22:10.607
I'll try to please you.

1308
01:22:11.107 --> 01:22:12.727
I'm like Pepe.

1309
01:22:13.027 --> 01:22:15.027
I like him with diamonds.

1310
01:22:15.347 --> 01:22:17.127
Now he's missed his chance.

1311
01:22:17.567 --> 01:22:21.867
So I guess I'll have to go downtown
and get my personal attention to Madame

1312
01:22:21.947 --> 01:22:23.087
Hardback.

1313
01:22:24.187 --> 01:22:25.727
What steamer?

1314
01:22:26.087 --> 01:22:28.167
The Ville d'Alge, 10 o'clock.

1315
01:22:28.247 --> 01:22:30.207
Good. Make the reservation.

1316
01:22:30.967 --> 01:22:32.387
Are you leaving?

1317
01:22:33.067 --> 01:22:35.627
I suppose you won't stay for the funeral.

1318
01:22:38.687 --> 01:22:40.587
Four, first class.

1319
01:22:40.787 --> 01:22:43.047
Oh, send up some whiskey and soda.

1320
01:22:45.067 --> 01:22:46.507
You'll have a drink.

1321
01:22:46.767 --> 01:22:48.367
Just a short one.

1322
01:22:48.447 --> 01:22:50.047
Make you feel better.

1323
01:23:01.847 --> 01:23:03.267
Anything wrong?

1324
01:23:04.087 --> 01:23:07.387
Why don't you sing? Why don't
you mind your own business?

1325
01:23:07.467 --> 01:23:10.987
I am. Only I just thought
you might be interested.

1326
01:23:11.067 --> 01:23:12.607
I'm going downtown.

1327
01:23:12.947 --> 01:23:14.727
What for? I'm like you.

1328
01:23:14.807 --> 01:23:15.767
I'm bored.

1329
01:23:15.847 --> 01:23:17.287
Anything in your mind?

1330
01:23:17.367 --> 01:23:19.207
Just to look things over.

1331
01:23:19.527 --> 01:23:21.147
When are you going? Now.

1332
01:23:21.227 --> 01:23:22.667
No use to see a lawyer about it.

1333
01:23:22.747 --> 01:23:24.487
Do me a favor? Sure.

1334
01:23:24.567 --> 01:23:26.187
I want you to deliver a letter.

1335
01:23:26.267 --> 01:23:28.385
I'd take anything that isn't loaded.

1336
01:23:29.667 --> 01:23:31.727
Okay. I get the idea.

1337
01:23:31.807 --> 01:23:34.572
Maybe I don't look like
Cupid, but I'll manage.

1338
01:23:35.187 --> 01:23:36.567
Ben and Babel,

1339
01:23:36.947 --> 01:23:38.687
go to the servant's entrance.

1340
01:23:38.767 --> 01:23:42.207
Give someone a good tip and tell
them you've got to have an answer.

1341
01:23:42.287 --> 01:23:43.127
Don't worry.

1342
01:23:43.207 --> 01:23:45.347
I won't come back empty-handed.

1343
01:23:45.907 --> 01:23:47.627
I'll wait for you at your house.

1344
01:23:47.707 --> 01:23:49.127
I'll be back in two hours.

1345
01:23:49.207 --> 01:23:50.047
Tell Tanya.

1346
01:23:50.127 --> 01:23:51.227
Good luck.

1347
01:23:58.987 --> 01:24:00.667
What time is it?

1348
01:24:01.127 --> 01:24:02.647
Nine o'clock.

1349
01:24:03.127 --> 01:24:04.127
So?

1350
01:24:04.727 --> 01:24:05.787
Morning.

1351
01:24:05.907 --> 01:24:07.847
Sun is out. Oh.

1352
01:24:08.247 --> 01:24:10.047
I slept all that time?

1353
01:24:11.487 --> 01:24:12.407
Carlos?

1354
01:24:12.487 --> 01:24:14.247
He hasn't come back.

1355
01:24:14.407 --> 01:24:15.887
He hasn't come back?

1356
01:24:15.967 --> 01:24:18.027
I sat up all night.

1357
01:24:18.147 --> 01:24:19.627
He can't be careful himself.

1358
01:24:19.707 --> 01:24:23.147
I'd like to see him back with
what I've got to tell him.

1359
01:24:23.367 --> 01:24:26.087
This time I'll make him listen to me.

1360
01:24:26.967 --> 01:24:28.487
Poor Carlos.

1361
01:24:30.427 --> 01:24:32.687
Same old story.

1362
01:24:33.627 --> 01:24:35.527
Well, life is like that.

1363
01:24:35.607 --> 01:24:36.367
Yeah.

1364
01:24:36.447 --> 01:24:40.682
And we're dumb enough to hang on
because we don't want the story to end.

1365
01:24:41.987 --> 01:24:42.987
Smart.

1366
01:24:44.367 --> 01:24:46.947
Is Pepe here? What do you want?

1367
01:24:47.027 --> 01:24:48.787
We've been looking for you everywhere.

1368
01:24:48.867 --> 01:24:50.127
Why weren't you at home?

1369
01:24:50.207 --> 01:24:53.107
Because I'm here. What do you want, Lobby?

1370
01:24:54.127 --> 01:24:55.707
I must speak to you alone.

1371
01:24:55.787 --> 01:24:58.027
What's the mind with us?
Have we got smallpox?

1372
01:24:58.107 --> 01:24:59.307
It's all right. You can talk.

1373
01:24:59.387 --> 01:25:00.767
Pepe, I'm ashamed of myself.

1374
01:25:00.847 --> 01:25:02.107
What's new about that?

1375
01:25:02.187 --> 01:25:03.487
Oh, it's worse than you think.

1376
01:25:03.567 --> 01:25:06.107
I doubt it. Go ahead and insult me.

1377
01:25:06.187 --> 01:25:08.507
I deserve it. You flatter yourself.

1378
01:25:08.587 --> 01:25:10.647
It's about the letter
from Pierrot's mother.

1379
01:25:10.727 --> 01:25:14.087
I brought it and gave it to Aisha,
but I didn't know it was from the police.

1380
01:25:14.167 --> 01:25:16.887
If I had known the letter was written
by Regis, I wouldn't have done it.

1381
01:25:16.967 --> 01:25:18.487
Never! Go on.

1382
01:25:19.087 --> 01:25:21.734
It was really a woman
who gave me the letter.

1383
01:25:22.167 --> 01:25:25.107
If I had known the truth,
I wouldn't have touched it.

1384
01:25:25.187 --> 01:25:28.667
I'm an informer. Yes, but I
wouldn't have done a thing like that.

1385
01:25:28.747 --> 01:25:30.467
Oh, you're only half an informer.

1386
01:25:30.547 --> 01:25:32.147
The other half is all right.

1387
01:25:32.227 --> 01:25:33.767
Oh, that's why I'm here.

1388
01:25:33.847 --> 01:25:34.847
For what?

1389
01:25:35.267 --> 01:25:37.907
Oh, I couldn't stand it any longer.

1390
01:25:38.147 --> 01:25:40.747
Forgive me, Pepe. All
right, stop groveling.

1391
01:25:40.827 --> 01:25:43.747
It makes me sick. I want you
to have a good opinion of me.

1392
01:25:43.827 --> 01:25:44.747
So?

1393
01:25:44.827 --> 01:25:46.707
I want you to believe me.

1394
01:25:46.787 --> 01:25:48.027
That's why I'm here.

1395
01:25:48.107 --> 01:25:50.427
To tell you they got Carlos.

1396
01:25:50.507 --> 01:25:51.007
What?

1397
01:25:51.087 --> 01:25:52.667
What about Carlos?

1398
01:25:52.887 --> 01:25:54.467
The police took him.

1399
01:25:54.547 --> 01:25:56.347
How much did you sell him for?

1400
01:25:56.427 --> 01:25:58.747
I wouldn't be here if I'd sold him.

1401
01:25:59.307 --> 01:26:01.467
First Pierrot, then Carlos.

1402
01:26:02.187 --> 01:26:04.887
with runs in threes.
Your turn will be next, Pepe.

1403
01:26:04.967 --> 01:26:06.287
Don't be so sure.

1404
01:26:06.367 --> 01:26:07.847
So they arrested him.

1405
01:26:07.927 --> 01:26:08.907
Who did it?

1406
01:26:08.987 --> 01:26:10.127
Inspector Louven.

1407
01:26:10.207 --> 01:26:12.767
There were about a dozen
of them surrounded him.

1408
01:26:12.847 --> 01:26:14.127
Was there any shooting?

1409
01:26:14.207 --> 01:26:17.247
No, no. They managed very
quietly in a nice way.

1410
01:26:17.327 --> 01:26:18.607
What did you have to do with it?

1411
01:26:18.687 --> 01:26:21.167
I was at the police station
when they brought Carlos in.

1412
01:26:21.247 --> 01:26:23.047
I had a chance to see him in his cell.

1413
01:26:23.127 --> 01:26:25.427
He gave me a letter,
the one you had given him.

1414
01:26:25.507 --> 01:26:27.147
He told me to take it to the hotel.

1415
01:26:27.227 --> 01:26:30.087
Every time there's a letter,
he's the one that brings it.

1416
01:26:30.167 --> 01:26:32.107
It looks funny to me. Be quiet.

1417
01:26:32.187 --> 01:26:34.587
I am to be quiet while you
write letters to other women.

1418
01:26:34.667 --> 01:26:36.767
Never mind that. You
never wrote a letter to me.

1419
01:26:36.847 --> 01:26:37.847
Shut up!

1420
01:26:38.527 --> 01:26:40.827
So you went to the hotel with the letter.

1421
01:26:40.907 --> 01:26:42.467
I did it for you, Pepe.

1422
01:26:42.547 --> 01:26:44.567
Did you get it? What?

1423
01:26:44.847 --> 01:26:45.967
The answer.

1424
01:26:46.047 --> 01:26:48.347
Oh, she wanted to write
you, but she couldn't.

1425
01:26:48.427 --> 01:26:51.487
She's being closely watched,
but she expects you this morning.

1426
01:26:51.567 --> 01:26:53.187
You can go down without any risk.

1427
01:26:53.267 --> 01:26:56.107
Go to the service entrance
in the back of the hotel.

1428
01:26:56.187 --> 01:26:57.827
She'll be watching from her window.

1429
01:26:57.907 --> 01:26:58.907
Is that all?

1430
01:26:58.987 --> 01:27:02.107
Well, she wanted to come up,
but she couldn't get away.

1431
01:27:02.187 --> 01:27:04.167
You call. I told you to shut up.

1432
01:27:04.847 --> 01:27:05.927
Go on.

1433
01:27:06.007 --> 01:27:08.419
She's waiting for me to bring the answer.

1434
01:27:08.507 --> 01:27:10.067
What shall I tell her?

1435
01:27:10.187 --> 01:27:12.287
Oh, she's waiting for it.

1436
01:27:12.367 --> 01:27:13.367
Yes.

1437
01:27:13.827 --> 01:27:15.687
I'll take the answer myself.

1438
01:27:16.087 --> 01:27:17.647
You wait here.

1439
01:27:19.647 --> 01:27:21.747
But, baby. Don't worry.

1440
01:27:21.927 --> 01:27:25.627
My friends will take good
care of you till I come back.

1441
01:27:27.407 --> 01:27:29.027
But she expect me.

1442
01:27:29.547 --> 01:27:30.547
What?

1443
01:27:31.807 --> 01:27:32.827
Nothing.

1444
01:27:33.947 --> 01:27:35.187
I'll wait.

1445
01:27:35.947 --> 01:27:38.587
Tell me, what about Carlos?

1446
01:27:39.387 --> 01:27:40.847
Didn't he say anything else?

1447
01:27:40.927 --> 01:27:41.947
Nothing.

1448
01:27:42.087 --> 01:27:43.347
Did they search him?

1449
01:27:43.427 --> 01:27:44.447
Yes.

1450
01:27:44.587 --> 01:27:45.467
Oh.

1451
01:27:45.547 --> 01:27:47.207
Then they took away the 5,000.

1452
01:27:47.287 --> 01:27:48.287
Yes.

1453
01:27:49.767 --> 01:27:52.607
You're sure he didn't
slip the 5,000 to you?

1454
01:27:52.687 --> 01:27:53.507
No.

1455
01:27:53.587 --> 01:27:54.487
You're sure?

1456
01:27:54.567 --> 01:27:55.607
My boy, the one.

1457
01:27:55.687 --> 01:27:56.707
Your what?

1458
01:27:57.087 --> 01:28:00.087
Levin took the money.
I saw him put it in his desk.

1459
01:28:01.767 --> 01:28:04.587
You said Gabi couldn't ride
because she was watched.

1460
01:28:04.667 --> 01:28:05.267
Yes.

1461
01:28:05.347 --> 01:28:07.827
But in a little while
she'll be able to see me.

1462
01:28:07.907 --> 01:28:09.613
On the key back of the hotel.

1463
01:28:09.747 --> 01:28:11.047
That's funny.

1464
01:28:11.627 --> 01:28:13.047
He's going to move away.

1465
01:28:13.127 --> 01:28:14.387
Oh, I see.

1466
01:28:14.747 --> 01:28:16.247
But why couldn't she ride to me?

1467
01:28:16.327 --> 01:28:17.247
He was there.

1468
01:28:17.327 --> 01:28:19.092
And how could she talk to you?

1469
01:28:19.707 --> 01:28:21.727
Because... Because you don't know.

1470
01:28:22.007 --> 01:28:25.007
Now there is another thing
that doesn't fit in your story.

1471
01:28:25.087 --> 01:28:28.707
How was Louvain able to
take 5,000 francs from Carlos

1472
01:28:30.167 --> 01:28:32.007
I don't know. I thought of 5,000.

1473
01:28:32.087 --> 01:28:35.567
Now something else. You think Carlos
is dumb enough to give you my letter?

1474
01:28:35.647 --> 01:28:37.387
All joking aside. But you are the letter.

1475
01:28:37.467 --> 01:28:40.027
You think me so stupid as to
believe he would give it to you?

1476
01:28:40.107 --> 01:28:42.087
All joking aside. I give you my word.

1477
01:28:42.167 --> 01:28:45.187
You wanted to bring her my answer,
and then I would go down to see her.

1478
01:28:45.267 --> 01:28:49.707
Yes. For a woman who is closely watched,
it's funny the way she can do things.

1479
01:28:49.787 --> 01:28:51.427
Now I've laughed enough. You hear me?

1480
01:28:51.507 --> 01:28:53.547
I'm fool laughing. I'm
the head of my father.

1481
01:28:53.627 --> 01:28:55.587
Word of it. He was guillotine.

1482
01:28:55.827 --> 01:28:57.967
Carlos was arrested. I told you.

1483
01:28:58.047 --> 01:28:59.871
You had my letter. That's true.

1484
01:29:00.027 --> 01:29:02.387
After that it beats. But
after that nothing beats.

1485
01:29:02.467 --> 01:29:03.487
Now tell me what happened.

1486
01:29:03.567 --> 01:29:04.947
Oh my God, nothing.

1487
01:29:05.047 --> 01:29:07.387
Shall I break your neck
to refresh your memory?

1488
01:29:07.467 --> 01:29:08.807
I'll tell Pepe.

1489
01:29:09.227 --> 01:29:09.827
Hey.

1490
01:29:09.907 --> 01:29:11.467
Slimane planned it all. Yeah?

1491
01:29:11.547 --> 01:29:12.787
He told me to come to you.

1492
01:29:12.867 --> 01:29:14.487
Go on. He thinks you'll come down.

1493
01:29:14.567 --> 01:29:15.947
Then? The hotel is surrounded.

1494
01:29:16.027 --> 01:29:17.787
They're waiting. Did you see the girl?

1495
01:29:17.867 --> 01:29:19.867
No. Why didn't she come up yesterday?

1496
01:29:19.947 --> 01:29:21.467
He told her you've been killed.

1497
01:29:21.547 --> 01:29:22.900
That's what she thinks.

1498
01:29:23.047 --> 01:29:25.635
She's leaving this
morning on Ville d'Alger.

1499
01:29:25.807 --> 01:29:27.727
Slimane planned the whole thing.

1500
01:29:29.087 --> 01:29:30.247
Is that all?

1501
01:29:30.327 --> 01:29:31.327
Yes.

1502
01:29:32.107 --> 01:29:33.107
Thanks.

1503
01:29:46.347 --> 01:29:48.107
You can't do it, Pepe.

1504
01:29:48.187 --> 01:29:50.487
You can't leave me. What have I done?

1505
01:29:51.207 --> 01:29:53.647
It has nothing to do with you, Ennis.

1506
01:29:53.827 --> 01:29:56.687
You're a good kid,
but this can't be helped.

1507
01:29:58.767 --> 01:30:00.507
I won't let you do it. I won't let you.

1508
01:30:00.587 --> 01:30:02.507
You'll be killed. Well,
blame it on the castor.

1509
01:30:02.587 --> 01:30:06.007
It's for her. You don't care about anything
else, or you're throwing away a lie.

1510
01:30:06.087 --> 01:30:08.247
Well, it's my own lie.
Oh, don't do it, Pepe.

1511
01:30:08.327 --> 01:30:10.427
Don't go. Listen to me.

1512
01:30:10.507 --> 01:30:11.507
Pepe!

1513
01:31:52.147 --> 01:31:54.047
Wind.

1514
01:32:47.307 --> 01:32:49.487
We didn't expect you.

1515
01:32:51.327 --> 01:32:52.767
He's gone to the boat.

1516
01:32:52.847 --> 01:32:54.627
You expect me to believe that?

1517
01:32:54.707 --> 01:32:56.747
He's going away with her.

1518
01:32:59.547 --> 01:33:01.807
So you're the one to betray him.

1519
01:33:01.887 --> 01:33:03.947
You couldn't wait to run to me.

1520
01:33:04.027 --> 01:33:07.507
You call it love, but it means you'd
kill him before you'd let him go free.

1521
01:33:07.587 --> 01:33:08.767
That's what you've done.

1522
01:33:08.847 --> 01:33:11.747
As sure as if you'd
held a gun in your hands.

1523
01:33:11.827 --> 01:33:13.527
I couldn't let him go.

1524
01:33:13.607 --> 01:33:15.587
I couldn't lose him.

1525
01:33:17.347 --> 01:33:19.807
I thought I'd figured all the moves.

1526
01:33:21.707 --> 01:33:23.067
I didn't think of you.

1527
01:33:23.147 --> 01:33:24.467
There's just time.

1528
01:33:26.027 --> 01:33:29.498
In a few more minutes, it might
have been out of our hands.

1529
01:33:30.467 --> 01:33:31.267
Don't go.

1530
01:33:31.347 --> 01:33:33.427
Give him a chance. I did. But you knew.

1531
01:33:33.507 --> 01:33:36.727
You planned it this way. So he'd
walk into a trap and he's done it.

1532
01:33:36.807 --> 01:33:38.767
With your help. Come on.

1533
01:34:38.867 --> 01:34:42.087
You know, the pleasant thing
about traveling is going back home,

1534
01:34:42.167 --> 01:34:43.787
and then going away again.

1535
01:34:44.387 --> 01:34:47.047
Well, I had a good time,
didn't you, Andre?

1536
01:34:47.387 --> 01:34:48.387
Me?

1537
01:34:49.767 --> 01:34:52.307
I never laughed so much in my life.

1538
01:35:06.007 --> 01:35:10.867
You see, Pepe, we meet
at the appointed time.

1539
01:35:11.447 --> 01:35:15.207
To tell the truth, I almost
missed the appointment.

1540
01:35:18.747 --> 01:35:20.167
Not here.

1541
01:35:20.287 --> 01:35:21.807
As you wish.

1542
01:35:22.127 --> 01:35:24.687
I can't refuse an old friend.

1543
01:35:59.227 --> 01:36:02.167
All ashore, who goes ashore?

1544
01:36:24.947 --> 01:36:27.187
Let me wait here until it leaves.

1545
01:36:28.067 --> 01:36:29.867
There's not much to ask.

1546
01:36:31.427 --> 01:36:33.087
I can't get away.

1547
01:36:35.067 --> 01:36:36.947
I know I can trust you.

1548
01:36:37.587 --> 01:36:38.940
I know I can trust you.

1549
01:37:29.127 --> 01:37:31.027
Gat!

1550
01:37:37.447 --> 01:37:38.647
Gat!

1551
01:37:58.587 --> 01:38:00.287
I'm sorry, Pepe.

1552
01:38:00.367 --> 01:38:02.767
He thought you were going to escape.

1553
01:38:06.147 --> 01:38:11.447
And so I have, my friend.

1554
01:38:47.787 --> 01:38:49.727
Thank you.

